\par\par \b \uc2  Sing dlr holding up, won off lows, govt steps eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2001\par 04:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0225 GMT - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar recouped some lost ground after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this week kept corporate dollar demand subdued and prompted some players to unwind long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  - Some U.S. names spotted selling dollar, but buying on dips provided some support at around 1.8075. \par \par \uc2  - Dealers said MAS not in market so far on Wednesday, but they did not expect Sing dollar to fall past 11-year low of 1.8230, level where \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during London trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  - Korean won -2 off lows as yen holds above 126. Market reluctant to push local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down amid talk \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered dollars from 1,355 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  - Officials said government would take steps if needed to stabilise won. But it would not announce support measures for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday as previously expected. \par \par \uc2  - Indonesian rupiah weaker on local corporate dollar demand in thin trade. Most deals cut within 10,450-10,465 range. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta dealers say no signs of dollar sales by state banks which may encourage players to bid up dollar to test 10,500. 10,425-10,500 trading range expected for day. \par \par \uc2  - Bank Indonesia says rupiah would get worse without its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support it. \par \par \uc2 Dokument 