\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Sagging yen casts shadow. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2001\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 2 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under renewed pressure on Monday as the yen struggled at fresh 30-month lows, raising expectations of further weakness across the region. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan's quarterly "tankan" survey, showing business sentiment had worsened, coupled with conflicting comments from Japanese finance officials pulled the yen down to lows of around 126.65 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The euro also fell to new lows for the year below $0.8750 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar fell past its Asian crisis lows of 1.8150 while the baht was beaten down to lows not seen since March 1998. \par \par \uc2  The only exception was the rupiah which held steady at 30-month lows, drawing support from modest dollar sales by state banks, usually active on behalf of the Indonesian authorities. \par \par \uc2  Other central banks and governments in the region only attempted to slow the declines through verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  With the yen believed to be still far from a bottom despite its over nine percent decline since the begining of the year, most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were likely to see further downside. \par \par \uc2  "The yen weakness looks irretrievable and at the moment, that is the key catalyst for weakness in all the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jan Lee, chief strategist at HypoVereinsbank. \par \par \uc2  A chief dealer at a European bank said pessimism over Japanese economic performance and uncertainty about the euro zone monetary policy had fuelled safe-haven flows to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  He said even U.S. equity gloom was helping the dollar, as investors were repatriating funds from other markets to cover their losses. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar remained downcast after hitting lows of 1.8165 to the dollar against the backdrop of a weakening yen and corporate demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed much of its drop to the yen, with offshore parties out of London aggressively bidding up dollar/Sing in afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  They said solid buying interest for the U.S. dollar was still intact, most of which they reckoned was genuine demand related to M&A activities. \par \par \uc2  The apparent lack of any official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also generated speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have opted to keep out of the market given persistent demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  "Of course this is a 39-month low and very weak, but relative to what? The yen is falling way faster than the Sing dollar," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "They (authorities) can control how the Sing fluctuates but they can't do anything about the yen, or other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar is managed against an undisclosed trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , believed to include the yen, euro and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some analysts believe the MAS has already shifted its stance to neutral from a tightening bias, given deteriorating external demand, despite its statement last week that short-term fluctuations did not affect its policy stance. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT The baht was beaten down to 36-month lows around 45.20 weighed by weaker regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the uncertain economic picture at home. \par \par \uc2  It was kept from falling further after Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said he had asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to monitor baht movements to determine if there was any speculation behind its decline. But dealers saw the respite as short-lived. \par \par \uc2  Adding to the gloom, a business confidence survey by the Bank of Thailand showed Thai companies were less optimistic about the economic outlook for the second month in a row in February. \par \par \uc2  On the political front, Thailand's Constitutional Court begins hearing a graft case against Thaksin on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  If the court upholds a ruling Thaksin would face a five-year ban from politics. Thaksin said he would not attend the first day of the hearing. He is due to address the country and unveil an economic stimulus package in the evening. \par \par \uc2  The only support the baht found was extremely tight offshore liquidity, brokers said. Baht funding cost in the offshore market jumped, with the one-month forward rate at 65/75 satang per dollar against 30/50 earlier in day. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won ended at a near 30-month low despite repeated verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said its weakness was mainly due to the yen's breach of 125 after the release of the BOJ's tankan survey of business sentiment. The won has been tied to the yen for several weeks as Korea and Japan compete on the same key exports to the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Investors in Korea have been fretting over the speed of the yen's drop. Dealers in Singapore said dollar bids in the offshore non-deliverable forward market have also pressured the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Both the Finance Ministry and the Bank of Korea warned the market that they were watching it closely, reiterating that the won's sensitivity towards other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not desirable. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the authorities were not spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though state banks had sold dollars on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the authorities were unlikely to actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as Korea needs to keep its competitive edge in the face of slowing external demand. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso gapped down at the open and dipped to a session low of 49.83 from Friday's close of 49.51. \par \par \uc2  But profit-taking on dollar longs and a lack of dollar demand from local corporates provided some support at around the 49.80 level, helping the peso close at 49.77. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said the peso was likely to trend lower in line with other regionals with next psychological support seen at the 50 figure. \par \par \uc2  But charts showed the dollar might pull back a bit before testing 50 as it was deep in overbought territory with a reading of 91.53 on the 14-day relative strength index. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said commercial banks' non-performing loan ratio increased to 16 percent of total loans at the end of January from 15.10 percent in December. \par \par \uc2  It said it expected annual inflation in March to be between 6.5 percent and 7.0 percent. A Reuters poll earlier showed an average forecast of 6.8 percent, almost flat from the 6.7 percent rise in February. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR The Taiwan dollar stayed soft after hitting three-month lows of 32.965, due to the falling yen and a slide in Taiwan equities. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark TAIEX fell 3.3 percent, led by a sell-off in electronics shares. \par \par \uc2  "I think the Taiwan dollar should fall further because in real terms it is still overvalued compared with the won and the yen," a senior European bank trader in Hong Kong said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar has lagged losses in the yen and won, which are down more than nine percent and five percent respectively since the end of last year. \par \par \uc2  He said the Taiwan dollar was targeting a major psychological support of 33.00, a break of which would open the way to last year's lows of 33.20. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  Despite the yen-inspired falls in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupiah held steady on early dollar sales by state banks. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said state banks pumped in a small amount of only $5 million but that proved enough to deter dollar-starved local corporates wary of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also worked as overall trading volume was low, with less than $50 million dealt. \par \par \uc2  However, sentiment was negative on lingering political uncertainty and on negative news flow from the economic front. \par \par \uc2  Finance minister Prijadi Praptosuhardjo warned the 2001 budget deficit could be wider than the expected 3.7 percent of gross domestic product, because of a weak rupiah, high domestic interest rates and low world oil prices. \par \par \uc2  An official from the statistics bureau said 2001 annual inflation could exceed the 7.2 percent forecast in the budget. The bureau earlier announced March annual inflation growth at 10.62 percent, up from 9.14 percent in February. \par \par \uc2  Trade data also painted a dismal picture showing the February surplus shrank to $1.70 billion from $1.82 billion in January as exports eased and imports were flat. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0856 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan 