\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dollar falls beyond Asian crisis low. \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2001\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 2 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar buckled under 1.8150 to the U.S. dollar on Monday, falling beyond lows last seen during the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  It hit a low of 1.8165 in afternoon trade, down 0.7 percent from its late Friday levels of around 1.8030. It has lost more than four percent since the end of last year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the breach of 1.8150, last hit on January 8, 1998 according to Reuters data, exposed it to a decline towards decade-lows beyond 1.8300. \par \par \uc2  Its drop on Monday came amid further weakness in the yen and the Thai baht. There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think they'll (the MAS) come in at this point. Sentiment is just too weak for the Sing dollar," said a chief dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  After falling through 1.8100 psychological support in early trade, the Singapore dollar won a mild respite before extending its decline as European markets opened and the yen revisited 30-month lows around 126.65 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the market had grown increasingly bearish amid reduced prospects for the Singapore economy, the fragile yen and euro and anticipation of further M&A-related outflows. \par \par \uc2  But they said the Singapore dollar was by no means isolated in its troubles and the fall owed much to an inevitable spillover effect from other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The MAS uses the Singapore dollar exchange rate as its main policy tool, managing it against an undisclosed trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts say the basket includes the U.S. dollar, the euro, the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4202shg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
