\par\par \b \uc2  Sing dlr hits fresh 39-month low, baht near 45.20. \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2001\par 07:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0540 GMT - The Singapore dollar briefly breached the 1.8100 psychological barrier amid weakness in the yen and other regionals, and with no immediate sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - Dealers said Sing dollar likely to take brief breather before testing next support at 1.8150, last seen in January 1998. \par \par \uc2  - Most analysts believe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely as Sing dollar weakness on back of softer yen and other regionals, which components of Singapore's trade-weighted basket. \par \par \uc2  - But some analysts say MAS more concerned about imported inflation than export competitiveness, and may eventually step in if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  decline jeopardises its 2001 inflation forecast of under 2.0 percent. - Convincing break of 1.8150 to take Sing to 10-year lows, with next support seen within 1.8280-1.8300 range. Some pullback likely as U.S. dollar overbought with 14-day RSI reading of 84.40. \par \par \uc2  - Thai baht mired at 36-month lows around 45.20 despite Prime Minister Thaksin's comment that he had asked \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to monitor its movement to see if speculation behind recent weakness. \par \par \uc2  - Bangkok dealers said wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  checks and queries could slow baht's decline, but only temporarily. \par \par \uc2  - Thaksin's comment conflicts with last week's finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments that suggested no abnormal speculation and no worries over recent baht declines. \par \par \uc2  - Indonesian rupiah steady despite yen-inspired falls in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , thanks to early modest dollar sales by state banks, keeping dollar-starved local corporates at bay and trading volumes thin. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta dealers spotted state banks selling $5 million, with total turnover by midday only $30 million. \par \par \uc2  - Local newspaper report saying Japan agreed in principle to reschedule Indonesia's $2.5 billion debt seen also helping, but overall sentiment negative on political uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  - Korean won -2 harbouring just above 1,340 in choppy trade after skidding to 29-month lows of 1341.7. \par \par \uc2  - Yen's recovery from 30-month lows against dollar seen helping won but dealers say sentiment still depressed on poor March trade performance reflecting slowing exports. \par \par \uc2  - Korean finance ministry says closely watching \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and close link between yen and won not desirable.. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4202sga\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
