\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Singapore MAS says no change in policy stance. \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 16:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 29 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) said on Thursday short term volatility in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not affect its policy stance, contrary to speculation it would shift to a neutral from tightening bias. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar slipped past the psychologically key 1.8000 mark against the U.S. dollar for the first time since January 12, 1998, raising speculation the MAS would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "In the short-term, merger and acquisition activities by local companies may cause volatility in the Singapore dollar," it said in a statement in reply to Reuters' queries. \par \par \uc2  The MAS said M&A activities did not affect the fundamentals of the Singapore economy. \par \par \uc2  "Therefore, any short-term volatility in the Singapore dollar will not affect MAS' policy stance on the Singapore dollar, or the policy band," it added. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar had been struggling under a barrage of bad news from the weaker euro to the Singapore Telecommunications Ltd proposed purchase of Australia's Cable & Wireless Optus . \par \par \uc2  SingTel is 78 percent owned by the Singapore government. \par \par \uc2  In February, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  restated its stance that it would maintain its current monetary policy and continue to allow a gradual, modest appreciation of the Singapore dollar on a trade-weighted basis. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said on Thursday the Sing dollar had moved below the policy band in their simulated trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  baskets, heightening the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  MAS reiterated that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary to dampen excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar exchange rate movements, including movements arising from the funding of corporate M&A activities. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said: "Apart from the bank counterparties which MAS deals with for its money market and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , MAS does not transact \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  with any other commercial entity." MAS said that it manages the Singapore dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and not against the U.S. dollar or any other bilateral exchange rate. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3t02wxh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
