\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore MAS Declines To Comment On SGD Fall To New Low \b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 17:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore late Thursday declined to comment on the Singapore dollar's fall to a fresh three-year low. \par \par \uc2  In written reply to questions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had nothing further to add to a statement issued Monday to Dow Jones Newswires, in which it said: "We do not comment on specific market movements in the Singapore dollar." \par \par \uc2  Monday's statement also said that the MAS believes any short-term volatility in the Singapore dollar "will not" affect its declared, moderately tight monetary policy stance or the undisclosed band within which it manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Any short-term volatility in the Singapore dollar will not affect MAS' policy stance on the Singapore dollar, or the policy band," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said. \par \par \uc2  The MAS also reiterated Monday that it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if required, "to dampen excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar exchange rate movements," but failed to carry out its threat, encouraging some speculators to drive the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower all week. This triggered stop-loss buying by banks and local companies who had been expecting the MAS to arrest the local dollar's descent. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's plunge to another 38-month low, without opposition from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fueled speculation that the MAS may have subtly eased its monetary policy stance from moderately tight to neutral. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar crested psychological resistance at S$1.8000, hitting a high of S$1.8040, as market participants tested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve to carry out its oft-repeated threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves become too volatile. \par \par \uc2  This was the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's lowest level since January 1998 - the depths of the Asian financial crisis - when it touched S$1.8170. \par \par \uc2  However, it recovered by late afternoon, as jittery bankers and investors sold U.S. dollars amid \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears. Light U.S. dollar selling by two local banks during Asian trading also aided the Singapore dollar's recovery, but the selling wasn't aggressive enough to suggest that it was at the MAS' behest, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 1519 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8000. \par \par \uc2  Following is the full text of the MAS statement issued Monday, which it repeated late Thursday: \par \par \uc2  "We do not comment on specific market movements in the Singapore dollar. MAS manages the Singapore dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and not against the U.S. dollar or any other bilateral exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "Over the medium to long term, we expect the trade-weighted Singapore dollar exchange rate to reflect the fundamentals of the Singapore economy. In the short term, M&A activities by local companies may cause volatility in the Singapore dollar. But these M&A activities do not affect the fundamentals of the Singapore economy. Therefore any short term volatility in the Singapore dollar will not affect MAS' policy stance on the Singapore dollar, or the policy band. \par \par \uc2  "As MAS stated in its press answer on 5 March, MAS will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary to dampen excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar exchange rate movements, including movements arising from the funding of corporate M&A activities. \par \par \uc2  "Apart from the bank counterparties which MAS deals with for its money market and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , MAS does not transact \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  with any other commercial entity." \par \par \uc2  -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809; amit.prakash@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3t01e7g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
