\par\par \b \uc2  US Dlr Hits New 38-Month High Of S$1.8040; Local Bks Buy \b0\par\par\uc2 154 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 07:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The U.S. dollar rose to yet another 38-month high of S$1.8040 against the Singapore dollar Thursday, on buying by a large local bank, dealer said. \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to abstain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bank that bought the U.S. dollars often acts as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's proxy in defending the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "We are in uncharted territory and the next resistance seems to be the January 1998 high of 1.8150," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  However, with market participants wary of possible MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar retreated from its latest high and was quoted at S$1.8020 at 0604 GMT (1:04 a.m. EST). \par \par \uc2  -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809; amit.prakash@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3t01d78\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
