\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Sharply Late But Off New 38-Mo Low \b0\par\par\uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar fell to a new 38-month low of S$1.8040 to the U.S. dollar Thursday on selling trigged by a large local bank, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But light buying by other local banks at around the S$1.80 level amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the U.S. dollar's gains in late trading, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Some traders suggest two local banks may have acted on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out the volatility. \par \par \uc2  Around 0817 GMT (3.17 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7995, up from S$1.7933 late Wednesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  In a volatile trading day, the U.S. dollar breached several technical levels as a local bank, which often acts on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the Singapore dollar, bought U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  "We are in uncharted territory and the next resistance seems to be the January 1998 high of 1.8150," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts and dealers say that the reluctance of the MAS to defend the local dollar, even though its recent decline has outpaced that of the yen, points to a likely rethink of its declared policy of facilitating a gradual and modest appreciation of the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The MAS manages the Singapore dollar exchange rate against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the country's major trading partners and competitors. It maintains the trade-weighted exchange rate within an undisclosed band. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has "been out of the band for about two weeks now," said Rebecca Patterson, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with J.P. Morgan in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "It (the MAS) sees the move caused by things outside its control, and because Singapore's growth is also weakening, it could be that its moving towards a more neutral policy stance," she added. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In fact, Patterson says that despite its "rhetoric" about a strong\par local dollar, MAS has remained neutral this year. This perhaps explains\par the Singapore dollars decent from S$1.7318 at the beginning of this\par year.\par - - 29/03/01 08-39G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The action in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market also affected Singapore bonds, where\par trading was thin and yields were higher in late trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yield on the 10-year bond ended unchanged at 3.62%, while the\par seven-year bond yield rose two basis points to 3.46%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yield on the five-year Government paper rose three basis point to\par 3.09%. The two-year bond ended at 2.41%, up one basis point.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are pre-settlement closing bids and are subject to minor\par changes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Historic bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's Web site:\par (https://secure.mas.gov.sg/dataroom/dataroom_findbindex.htm  l).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, the most liquid seven-year swap\par offer was at 3.51%, unchanged from late Wednesday. The 10-year swap\par offer was up two basis points to 3.72%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between the two- and 10-year swaps was 106 basis points,\par from 105 basis points Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                  Late Thursday      Late Wednesday\par                  bid      offer     bid     offer\par Overnight        1.2500%  1.3750%   1.2500%  1.5000%\par 3 Month          2.2250%  2.3750%   2.1250%  2.2500%\par 1 Year           2.3125%  2.4375%   2.1875%  2.3750%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Hasan Jafri, Dow Jones Newswires; 65/421-4828;\par hasan.jafri@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3t01dk8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
