\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rangebound as dlr bulls pause. \b0\par\par\uc2 980 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were trapped in a tight range late on Wednesday as the market took stock of the latest developments both outside and inside the region. \par \par \uc2  An earlier more bullish mood brought about by a firmer yen and surprisingly strong consumer confidence figures from the U.S. proved elusive. \par \par \uc2  U.S. consumer confidence level increased to 117 in March from February's 109.2, and upward revision from 106.8. The average forecast from economists was for a decline to 104.50. \par \par \uc2  "That's the first piece of good news in a long time. But the market will need more evidence to prove the U.S. economy has reached bottom before there will be a meaningful turnaround in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Syetarn Hansakul, economist at WestLB in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "In the near-term, I think there is room for further downside for the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar went through a choppy session, trapped between fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and speculation on and actual outflows as funds sold SingTel shares to buy Cable & Wireless Optus stocks. \par \par \uc2  Indonesian rupiah was clouded by political uncertainty, but the downside was capped by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was a bit out of sync with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hitting 1.7955 - its worst level since August 31, 1998 - after a brief break earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  It was weighed by speculation of rising dollar demand following SingTel's successful bid of Optus. There was talk one telecom company bought up to US$200 million on Wednesday alone. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some funds were selling SingTel shares and buying Optus to take advantage of SingTel's options offered to the latter's shareholders. \par \par \uc2  But the downside was underpinned by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "But I noticed people were quick to take profits once the Sing dollar poked below 1.7950. We still think that's the level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT The baht kept a softer tone as local companies bought U.S. dollars to meet the end-month payment of their U.S dollar loan. One dealer in Bangkok estimated his bank saw them bid at 44.30-33 throughout the day and at least US$10 to 15 million orders were executed to the loan payment. \par \par \uc2  But the baht was refusing to retreat despite such pressure, in part because of the steady yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said 44.45 resistance for dlr/baht proved too high as it failed to break for the last two sessions. \par \par \uc2  Also supporting the baht was firmer baht funding cost in the offshore market. One-month forward rate rose to 15/18 satang per dollar from 12/17 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won edged up as a firmer yen and foreign buying of local stocks prompted trimming of some dollar longs. Dealers said expected month-end inflows from exporters also kept dollar bulls at bay. \par \par \uc2  But the trading range was tight and volumes were subdued amid undented pessimism over the slowing economy and uncertainty over direction of the yen. \par \par \uc2  Korea posted a month-on-month rise in current account surplus in February because of slowing imports, taken as another signal of slowing domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  February industrial production data is due on Thursday. A Reuters poll of 10 economist forecast output to remain flat from previous month, but rise by 5.3 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar nudged up in line with gains in the yen and won but its upside was capped by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to maintain the island's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Japan and Korea compete with Taiwan in several key export markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said month-end exporter inflows and settlement of recent foreign buying of local stocks have kept the Taiwan dollar firm. \par \par \uc2  However dealers said there was some caution in the market ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly policy meeting on Thursday. A Reuters poll of 10 economists and bankers showed all expected the bank to cut the key rates to boost economic activity. \par \par \uc2  The discount rate stands at 4.25 percent while the accommodation with collateral rate is at 4.625 percent. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia was heard selling a moderate amount of dollar at 10,400-10,420 in a thin and listless market to support the rupiah which was weighed by political uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  There was also talk that it had asked state companies to sell the dollar on Wednesday if the rupiah dropped sharply. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the move indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was nervous about political development following President Wahid's disappointing response to a parliament censure. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia also guided the benchmark one-month SBI rate higher to 15.58 percent at the auction from 15.24 percent last week to drain liquidity from the market. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0918 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.53\tab  122.67\tab    +0.94\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7938\tab  1.7916\tab    -0.12\par  Taiwan dlr     32.67\tab   32.68\tab    +0.03\par  Korean won   1304.60\tab 1309.50\tab    +0.38\par  Baht\tab      44.37\tab   44.36\tab    -0.02\par  Peso\tab      49.15\tab   48.63\tab    -1.06\par  Rupiah\tab 10350.00     10395.00\tab    +0.43\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.53\tab  114.45\tab    -5.83\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7938\tab  1.7365\tab    -3.19\par  Taiwan dlr     32.61\tab   32.90\tab    +0.89\par  Korean won   1304.60\tab 1277.00\tab    -2.12\par  Baht\tab      44.37\tab   43.70\tab    -1.51\par  Peso\tab      49.15\tab   50.75\tab    +3.26\par  Rupiah\tab 10350.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -8.50\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3s03156\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
