\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Wary of yen, though dollar overbought. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,106 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 04:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 26 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were keeping a wary eye on the yen in a market generally long dollars early on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar mustered some strength against the yen amid expectations of further safe haven flows to the U.S. But, with the end of the Japanese fiscal year nearing, the yen could show some resilience thanks to repatriation flows. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were likely to find some near-term support as the market was long dollars, making it vulnerable to corrections. \par \par \uc2  A steadier yen and possible gains on local bourses following Wall Street's stronger performance on Friday could spark unwinding of long dollars. \par \par \uc2  The domestic front was quiet, with Indonesian and Malaysian markets closed for public holidays. \par \par \uc2  But the Singapore dollar was under pressure after Singapore Telecommunications Ltd. made a formal bid for Australia's second largest telecoms carrier Cable & Wireless Optus Ltd. . However, analysts said most of the hedging for the deal was probably already completed. \par \par \uc2  The euro was still depressed after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  member Ernst Welteke sounded a hawkish note on Friday, fueling concerns the ECB could be sacrificing growth because of inflation fears. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar recoverd slightly after wallowing beneath 1.7940, a level not seen since August 31, 1998. \par \par \uc2  The latest upset was caused by news SingTel has made a bid for Australia's Optus at up to US$8.63 billion, what would be the largest foreign acquisition ever by a Singapore company. \par \par \uc2  "This is obviously a knee-jerk reaction to news, which is too big to ignore," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the earlier fall was intensified by stop-loss orders placed at 1.7900 in thin trading. \par \par \uc2  However, the market was wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the dollar/Sing was in overbought territory, with a 14-day relative strength index at 80.78. \par \par \uc2  But dealers expected profit-taking would bring the dollar back no further than 1.7850. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was on the defensive, cowering just above 44.46, its lowest level since March 1998. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the mood was bruised by the Sing dollar, which was nearing all-time lows. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the baht came under pressure after the Bank of Thailand said the country was due to repay $700 million to the IMF in the first quarter of this year. \par \par \uc2  But others said the news had limited impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Thailand could pay the debt from foreign reserves, as it did in March. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate in the offshore market eased to 22/27 satang per dollar from 39/50 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  Indonesian financial markets were closed to celebrate Muslim New Year and will resume trading on Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists in Singapore said they expected the rupiah to be supported around 10,500 this week after state-run Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA) stepped up its dollar sales on Friday to around $40-50 million. \par \par \uc2  IBRA started converting $500 million from recent asset sales on Thursday and dealers expected dollar offers to continue this week. \par \par \uc2  After IBRA converts those dollars, dealers said there was not much the government can do to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia governor Sjahril Sabirin said on Friday he was not sure if interest rates would be hiked at the SBI auction this week as the rates were already at a 20-month high. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won weakened on the back of a softer yen, though its downside was likely to be capped by profit-taking on dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said while the won is expected to slip further in the long term due to the yen's poor outlook, the market was still long dollars despite Friday's correction. A turnaround in the yen could spur the market to shed some of its long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Korea competes with Japan on a number of exports, making it vulnerable to the yen's movements. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the Korean economy has been showing signs of a sharp slowdown due to increasingly sluggish external demand. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry said on Friday it would follow a low interest rate policy in order to spur growth. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will meet on April 6 for its monthly monetary policy-setting meeting amid growing concerns over inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso opened lower at 49.25 per dollar in the onshore market compared with Friday's close of 49.135. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was weighed by dollar demand from importers, who became more active in dollar buying after it poked above 49.00 as they feared the peso may drop further. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, the peso's direction mostly hinged on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last week the country's net portfolio investments totalled $23.3 million up to the second week of March this year. \par \par \uc2  February saw a net outflow of $13.7 million compared with a net inflow of $31.40 million in January. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar edged lower in line with the yen, though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to cushion its fall. \par \par \uc2  In addition to the watchful \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hopes that the worse was over for U.S. technology stocks was also providing support for the local stocks, and in turn, the Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  However, the market was also abuzz about a possible rate cut from the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which said earlier it would hold a board meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The bank has made three rate cuts since late December, bringing its discount rate and accomodation with collaterol rate to 4.25 percent and 4.625 percent, respectively. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0200 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.52\tab  122.90\tab    -0.50\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7880\tab  1.7838\tab    -0.23\par  Taiwan dlr     32.79\tab   32.77\tab    -0.07\par  Korean won   1313.00\tab 1308.60\tab    -0.34\par  Baht\tab      44.33\tab   44.18\tab    -0.34\par  Peso\tab      49.26\tab   48.14\tab    -2.27\par  Rupiah\tab 10300.00     10373.00\tab    +0.71\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7999\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.52\tab  114.45\tab    -7.34\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7880\tab  1.7365\tab    -2.88\par  Taiwan dlr    