\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Singapore dlr fall may force MAS hand. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 09:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 26 (Reuters) - A sharp fall in the Singapore dollar to two-and-a-half year lows could soon force the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  hand of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  - even as it is seen becoming more relaxed about a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A struggling Japanese yen, gloom about Asia's prospects this year and the largest foreign takeover by a Singapore company have all helped push the Sing to where the market believes it is close to the top of the acceptable trading band for the MAS. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make its presence felt if the Sing dollar tries to move past Monday's low of 1.7945 to the U.S. dollar - its lowest since August 31, 1998. \par \par \uc2  "On the normal effective exchange rate basis, the dollar/Sing dollar is moving at the top of its band, and I don't think it will break 1.7950," DBS Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Philip Wee said. \par \par \uc2  "The Authority might come in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Monday's low came as \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  Telecommunications Ltd said it was going to spend up to $8.4 billion to buy Australian company Cable and Wireless Optus Ltd - even though it is likely that most, if not all, of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  component of the deal was carried out some time ago. \par \par \uc2  SPEED OF FALL A CONCERN \par \par \uc2  It is not only the outright level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the speed of its fall that has the market on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alert. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has fallen 1.15 percent against the dollar over the last week. In comparison, the yen has fallen 0.65 percent and the Indonesian rupiah has rallied 0.40 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The fall has been very rapid and that's why the market has to be cautious," UBS Warburg \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Mansoor Mohi-uddin said. \par \par \uc2  "No \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to see \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility." \par \par \uc2  The Sing is monitored against an unpublished trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which include the dollar, the euro, the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to ensure its competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  The MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally to make sure that the Sing dollar does not get out of sync with trading partners, both in terms of outright level and the velocity of its moves. \par \par \uc2  But the Singapore dollar is not alone in its woes - the yen has hit 22 month lows, the Australian dollar is at record lows, and the rupiah, Thai baht and Korean won have all fallen to levels last seen in the Asian economic crisis of 1997/98. \par \par \uc2  The Sing is down about 3.5 percent since the end of 2000, which compares favourably with falls of over eight percent in the yen and rupiah, and a 12.5 percent fall in the Aussie. \par \par \uc2  END OF TIGHTENING CYCLE NIGH? \par \par \uc2  The MAS announced on February 22 that it was sticking to its tightening bias to ward off inflation - a decision which surprised some given the global trend to easier monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  At the time, the MAS noted the trade weighted Sing was in the top half of its policy band. It was then trading around 1.7400. \par \par \uc2  The Authority said it would review its stance by mid-year or sooner, and even though the tighter bias could stave off \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility in the near term analysts believe monetary policy will soon shift to neutral to help counter weakening external demand. \par \par \uc2  Accordingly, the MAS is expected to become more tolerant of a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to keep the economy growing strongly. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters recently forecast economic growth in 2001 of 5.3 percent - just over half the 2000 growth rate of 9.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate remains Singapore's key counter cyclical tool. In our view, there is an 80 percent chance for a policy shift from gradual appreciation to neutral before mid-year," said Liang Chia-Lian, analyst at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  "Specifically, we are revising our end 2001 exchange rate forecast to S$1.80 from S$1.76 previously," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3q038sw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
