\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Falls To 38-Mo Low Vs USD At S$1.7920 \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 01:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar fell early Monday to a 38-month low against its U.S. counterpart at S$1.7920. \par \par \uc2  The fall is in response to confirmation that Singapore Telecommunications Ltd. (P.SGT) has launched a takeover bid for Australia's second largest telecommunications company, Cable & Wireless Optus Ltd. (A.CWO), valuing the company at up to A$17.2 billion. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Capital outflows would push the Singapore dollar down.\par - - 26/03/01 00-11G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The local dollar is at its lowest level since January 1998 - the\par depths of the Asian financial crisis - when it touched S$1.8170.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the fall in the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this morning is a knee-jerk\par response to the Singtel news, it has been steadily losing ground in\par recent weeks on growing concerns about the Japanese economy, which\par pushed the yen last week to a 22-month low against the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, the island-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par indicated recently it would provide foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  liquidity to\par prevent any volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the event of any one-time\par capital flows arising from mergers and acquisitions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders are also wary the MAS may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market by selling\par U.S. dollars to curb Singapore dollar weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A report issued last week by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's DBS Bank said the MAS might\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around S$1.7900 unless the U.S. dollar breaks above Y125.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DBS is one of a number of local banks that traders say sometimes act\par on behalf of the MAS.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Benjamin Pedley, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4485;\par ben.pedley@dowjones.com\par -0- 26/03/01 00-29G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3p01bol\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
