\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Easier on dollar strength, regional gloom. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,111 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 02:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 23 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased \par \par \uc2  early Friday as safe-haven flows from bearish equity markets \par \par \uc2  and a weaker outlook for the yen kept the dollar strong. \par \par \uc2      However, weekend short covering in recently battered \par \par \uc2  regional stock markets and wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could prompt trimming of long dollars. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A 3.69 percent gain on the technology-laden Nasdaq\tab   ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which rose only in the final minutes of trade, heightened hopes\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tech stocks have bottomed out and may help lift tech-sensitive\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par North Asian bourses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But with the yen expected to test much lower levels and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par most regionals facing their own economic and political woes,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players still preferred to take refuge in dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In early Asian trade, the yen was around fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 22-month lows against the dollar. The euro also looked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par feeble after hitting three-month lows overnight on concerns\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about euro zone growth after a weak reading in Germany's Ifo\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par business survey.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was supported by fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and dollar sales by IBRA, which said on Thursday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it had started converting $500 million from recent asset sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said IBRA sold around $20 million into the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Thursday and might be selling again on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The expectation of such conversion is limiting dollar's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upside for the moment as corporates await better levels to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buy," said IDEAglobal.com in a research note.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "But it will continue to require both the subsiding of real\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par end-quarter corporate dollar demand and more visible political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stability before dollar/rupiah bias has hope of sustained\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reversal," it said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the political front, President Abdurrahman Wahid said on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday he had no intention of resigning since to do so might\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trigger the break-up of Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At least 10 people were killed in the latest round of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ethnic riots in the country's Kalimantan province where\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hundreds died last month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won slipped to new 28-month lows as the yen teetered\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closer towards 124.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While rising local stocks cheered up gloomy sentiment a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bit, the won's fate still laid in the hands of the yen. Verbal\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by officials so far this week has proven\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fruitless, as dealers said those comments were not backed by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concerted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, analysts warned of a possible technical correction\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the dollar as the market was long on it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts showed the won still trapped in oversold territory\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with a reading of around 84 on the 14-day relative strength\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Looking ahead, though, analysts were still calling for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaker yen. JP Morgan said in a research report it saw the won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bottoming out around 1,330 by end-June, citing the global\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic slowdown, the limping tech sector and weaker yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso fell in line with weaker regionals, prompting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates to cover their future dollar requirements.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said there was some profit-taking in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars around the 49 level. But with no major factors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supporting the peso, a breach of the level was on cards.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary easing was further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par incentive to mark down the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its key overnight rates by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 50 basis points effective on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The cut takes the overnight borrowing rate to 10.0 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and lending rate to 12.25 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While the bank said it may ease further if the Federal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reserve continues to cut rates, it added that it was watching\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation numbers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite an overnight rise in U.S. tech stocks, the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar was still playing catch-up with the weakness in the yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While the market shrugged off recent economic data,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts said weaker-than-expected export orders and industrial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par output in February illustrated the extent at which Taiwan's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy was slowing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     JP Morgan forecast in a research report the Taiwan dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would reach 33.2 by end-June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar turned tail to hit fresh 31-month lows of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7905 overnight, as aggressive local bank selling triggered\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stop-loss orders around 1.7860-80.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers owed the underlying weakness to weaker regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and to speculation SingTel will seal a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deal to buy Australia's Optus soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar was only getting marginal support at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7990, last seen in August 31, 1998. A break of this bulwark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could open the way to all-time lows of 1.8150, hit on January\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8, 1998, according to Reuters data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But a swift and steep slide of the Sing dollar raised fears\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the Sing dollar may rebound to around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7820-30 as players were likely to take profit on dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charts showed the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was oversold with a 14-day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relative strength index reading of 77.56\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht cowered just above four-month lows of 44.46, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the government saying the weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not a cause for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concern.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said on Thursday the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht's weakness reflected a slowing world economy rather than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic problems.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts said repatriation by foreign investors to cover\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par losses at home and political risk also undermined the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thaksin was indicted in December by the National Counter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Corruption Commission for failing to declare some of his\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     If the Constitutional Court upholds the ruling, Thaksin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par faces a five-year ban from politics, which could throw domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par politics into turmoil.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Baht funding costs offshore firmed to 50/70 satang per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar from 20/35 on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Tight offshore baht liquidity and exporters' dollar selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could provide some marginal support, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0138 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.52\tab  123.97\tab    +0.36\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7850\tab  1.7885\tab    +0.20\par  Taiwan dlr     32.86\tab   32.86\tab    +0.00\par  Korean won   1318.00\tab 1318.60\tab    +0.05\par  Baht\tab      44.26\tab   44.43\tab    +0.38\par  Peso\tab      48.99\tab   48.41\tab    -1.18\par  Rupiah\tab 10370.00     10380.00\tab    +0.10\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.52\tab  114.45\tab    -7.34\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7850\tab  1.7365\tab    -2.72\par  Taiwan dlr     32.81\tab   32.90\tab    +0.27\par  Korean won   1318.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -3.11\par  Baht\tab      44.26\tab   43.70\tab    -1.27\par  Peso\tab      48.99\tab   50.75\tab    +3.59\par  Rupiah\tab 10370.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -8.68\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3n03hf6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
