\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Clouded by ailing yen, Wall St gloom. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 02:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 22 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  retained their bearish tone in early trade on Thursday as investors continue to look for good levels to buy the dollar amid gloom befalling Wall Street and the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yen to stay pressured as players take advantage of Japan's ultra-low interest rates, depressing regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Overall, the dollar is still pretty well-bid. External and domestic developments argue for long dollar positions," said a dealer at an Asian bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Some might be taking profits due to fears of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially in Korea and Taiwan, or because the market is a bit long of dollars. But I don't expect the dollar-buying trend to reverse anytime soon," he said. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's Ministry of Economic Affairs is due to publish data on February export orders and industrial output at 0230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  In January, the island's export orders were down 4.62 percent year-on-year while industrial output fell 13.98 percent on-year. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to hold an interest rate-setting meeting later in the day. Its top official said on Wednesday the monetary board was likely to cut key overnight rates by 50 basis points at the meeting. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was faced with the familiar depressing sight of a struggling yen and falling U.S. technology stocks. \par \par \uc2  UBS Warburg said in a research note the market was targeting 1,316, which is close to the 62 percent Fibonacci retracement of the dollar's fall between September 27, 1998 and January 10, 1999 on a weekly chart. The bank said its long-term target was 1,400. \par \par \uc2  But it warned that there was a possibility of a correction on a turnaround in the yen or \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While officials warned against further falls in the won on Wednesday, they did not seem to follow through on those comments with concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts said the government was likely to tolerate a weaker won, despite inflationary pressures, as Korea competes with Japan on a number of exports. \par \par \uc2  The won's 14-day relative strength index showed the dollar was overbought with a reading of over 75. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was likely to struggle amid a weaker yen and bearish sentiment towards the local bourse after the Nasdaq's overnight fall. \par \par \uc2  However, the market was expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in to cushion the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall. Taiwan has around $110 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interevenes frequently to smooth out any volatility in the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said despite this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Taiwan dollar should weaken given a slowing economy and softer yen. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan will release February industrial output and export orders at 0230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters on average expected industrial output to grow by 10.73 percent on year while export orders are expected to expand by 10.8 percent on year. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept a lid on the rupiah's falls, but strong corporate demand for dollars amid Indonesia's volatile political climate continued to weigh. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia hiked interest rates again on Wednesday as part of ongoing efforts to stem weakness in the rupiah. At its weekly SBI note auction, the benchmark one-month rate rose to 15.24 percent from the previous week's 14.97 percent. \par \par \uc2  On the political front, Indonesia's defence minister Mahfud M.D. said on Wednesday President Abdurrahman Wahid was ready to step down if parliament found he had violated the constitution. But he later backed away from his statement, saying Wahid would only resign if there were constitutional reasons. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar had no reprieve as aggressive dollar buying from British banks and offshore speculators knocked it down to fresh two-and-a-half year lows of 1.7850. Dealers said bears were cautious to push the Sing dollar lower, in part because charts showed dollar/Sing in overbought territory with a 14-day relative strength index reading at 79.09. \par \par \uc2  They said uncertainty over SingTel's bid to buy Australia's Optus and some concerns of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Sing underpinned the downside. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT The baht kept a softer tone after selling from local banks and foreign players triggered stop-loss dollar orders at 44.15, pushing it to four-and-a-half month lows around 44.24. \par \par \uc2  Weakness in the Sing dollar and the absence of exporters' bids for baht were threatening the next technical support of 44.435, the 38 percent Fibonacci retracement level of its steep January 19-April 5, 1998 drop. \par \par \uc2  Offshore baht funding costs firmed, with the one-month forward rate at 12/15 satang per dollar compared with 6.9/9.9 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso nudged lower against the dollar alongside the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hovering below 48.70. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market seemed to have factored in the likelihood of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cutting overnight rates further by 50 basis point later in the day. \par \par \uc2  Despite narrowing interest rate differentials between the peso and the U.S. dollar, the peso's downside should be limited due to improved political sentiment, they said. \par \par \uc2  "If the peso dips further, it would be because of the weakness in the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Domestic situation is quite calm now and that helps," said a dealer at a European bank in Manila. \par \par \uc2  "We noticed that the switching from local peso deposits to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits by locals, which is one of the major factors that affects the peso, has tapered off," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0124 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.69\tab  123.15\tab    -0.44\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7830\tab  1.7800\tab    -0.17\par  Taiwan dlr    32.835\tab  32.771\tab    -0.19\par  Korean won   1295.00\tab 1305.00\tab    +0.77\par  Baht\tab      44.26\tab   44.13\tab    -0.29\par  Peso\tab      48.76\tab   48.55\tab    -0.43\par  Rupiah\tab 10460.00     10405.00\tab    -0.53\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.69\tab  114.45\tab    -7.47\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7830\tab  1.7365\tab    -2.61\par  Taiwan dlr    32.835\tab  32.900\tab    +0.20\par  Korean won   1295.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.39\par  Baht\tab      44.26\tab   43.70\tab    -1.27\par  Peso\tab      48.76\tab   50.75\tab    +4.08\par  Rupiah\tab 10460.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -9.46\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3m03jfa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
