\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Range-bound ahead of Fed decision. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,057 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 03:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 20 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a mixed bag early Tuesday as profit-taking in dollar/yen provided some support but uncertainty ahead of the Federal Reserve policy meeting kept their recent ranges intact. \par \par \uc2  The yen had hit 22-month lows on Monday after the Bank of Japan announced it would set a target of keeping bank reserves at around five trillion yen - a "quantitative easing" that would allow interest rates to fall back to virtually zero. \par \par \uc2  Players heavily long in dollars later decided to book profits as the dollar neared overbought territory on the 14-day relative strength index while speculation increased on how deep the Fed would cut the interest rates. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll on Monday showed the market almost evenly split over whether the Fed will cut interest rates by 75 basis points or 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan has been under intense political pressure to counteract deflation after controversially abandoning its zero interest rate policy last August. \par \par \uc2  But skepticism that the move would solve Japan's more serious structural problems would keep the yen under pressure which would keep sentiment dampened for other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro was steady with overall trade in majors thinned by a local holiday in Japan. Players in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would also tread cautiously ahead of the Fed rate decision. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing Dollar was holding above 1.7700, with the market focusing on the outcome of SingTel 's bid for Australia's Optus . \par \par \uc2  "With the market still looking long of U.S. dollars we are concerned that any withdrawal by SingTel will lead to the U.S. dollar coming off sharply here," Mansoor Mohi-uddin, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  Bears had piled up sizable U.S. dollar long positions on speculation SingTel would buy the Australian company at around $7 billion. \par \par \uc2  The market was still less wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which threatens the 1.7800 support, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was on a healthy tone, holding above 44.00 after offshore players took profits on their U.S. dollar long positions. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the slowing economy and political risks pointed to a distress for the Thai stock market, thereby for the baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar was facing resistance at 44.150, with a break of this bulwark opening the way to near the November 26 high of 44.435, which also marks the 38 percent retracement of its steep January 18-April 5 1998 drop, on a weekly chart. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate in the offshore market eased to 8/13 satang per dollar from 10/12 in late Monday trading. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won recovered from a fresh 28-month low in line with gains in the yen but trade is likely to remain subdued ahead of the Fed rate decision. \par \par \uc2  Profit-taking in dollar/yen and overnight Nasdaq gains prompted players to trim their dollar longs against the won. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Korea will release the preliminary 2000 gross domestic product growth data at 0300 GMT. A recent Reuters poll showed economists on average expect the Korean economy to have contracted by nearly one percent in the fourth quarter from the third quarter. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO The peso was steady, aided by the steady yen and a mild recovery in January imports. \par \par \uc2  Philippines imports rose to $2.47 billion in January from $2.24 in December but it was still below year-ago levels. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the bounce from December showed a slowdown in exports, due to tapering world demand for electronics products, could soon be reversed, at least temporary. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said players were looking levels to sell the U.S. dollar above 48.50, which would underpin the peso. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was down as markets braced for protest rallies planned in the day by supporters of President Abdurrahman Wahid who is facing increasing pressure to step down amid corruption allegations. \par \par \uc2  Fears that the rallies led by the 40-million strong Nahdlatul Ulama, Indonesia's largest Muslim organisation, could add to the violence plaguing the country for the past several months were likely to keep the rupiah under pressure. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said given the political situation, moves like interest rate hikes and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was unlikely to give a lasting support to the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia said on Monday it would raise interest rates this week due to concerns over inflation and added that it had continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the ailing rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's recent fall through 10,000 to the U.S. dollar has unsettled officials, fearful that imported inflation could raise prices for Indonesia's millions of poor and spark more social unrest across the embattled country. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was hovering close to 32.80, its lowest since January 9 but dealers said rise in the yen and gains in U.S. tech stocks was likely to keep the downside limited. \par \par \uc2  They said expected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and foreign inflows in the domestic stocks market, with foreign investors buying T$8.327 billion in the last four sessions was also likely to provide support. \par \par \uc2  However, trade was likely to remain subdued with most players staying cautious ahead of the Fed policy meeting. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0234 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.78\tab  123.40\tab    +0.50\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7713\tab  1.7688\tab    -0.14\par  Taiwan dlr     32.78\tab   32.78\tab    -0.00\par  Korean won   1294.60\tab 1299.00\tab    +0.34\par  Baht\tab      43.90\tab   43.95\tab    +0.11\par  Peso\tab      48.46\tab   48.50\tab    +0.08\par  Rupiah\tab 10390.00     10325.00\tab    -0.63\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.78\tab  114.45\tab    -6.78\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7713\tab  1.7365\tab    -1.96\par  Taiwan dlr     32.73\tab   32.90\tab    +0.52\par  Korean won   1294.60\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.36\par  Baht\tab      43.90\tab   43.70\tab    -0.46\par  Peso\tab      48.46\tab   50.75\tab    +4.73\par  Rupiah\tab 10390.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -8.85\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3k03rc3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
