\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Range-bound ahead of Fed decision. \b0\par\par\uc2 901 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 03:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 20 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a \par \par \uc2  mixed bag early Tuesday as profit-taking in dollar/yen provided \par \par \uc2  some support but uncertainty ahead of the Federal Reserve \par \par \uc2  policy meeting kept their recent ranges intact. \par \par \uc2     The yen had hit 22-month lows on Monday after the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Japan announced it would set a target of keeping bank reserves \par \par \uc2  at around five trillion yen -- a "quantitative easing" that \par \par \uc2  would allow interest rates to fall back to virtually zero. \par \par \uc2      Players heavily long in dollars later decided to book \par \par \uc2  profits as the dollar neared overbought territory on the 14-day \par \par \uc2  relative strength index while speculation increased on how deep \par \par \uc2  the Fed would cut the interest rates. \par \par \uc2      A Reuters poll on Monday showed the market almost evenly \par \par \uc2  split over whether the Fed will cut interest rates by 75 basis \par \par \uc2  points or 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Japan has been under intense political pressure \par \par \uc2  to counteract deflation after controversially abandoning its \par \par \uc2  zero interest rate policy last August. \par \par \uc2      But skepticism that the move would solve Japan's more \par \par \uc2  serious structural problems would keep the yen under pressure \par \par \uc2  which would keep sentiment dampened for other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab   was steady with overall trade in majors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par thinned by a local holiday in Japan. Players in Asian\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would also tread cautiously ahead of the Fed rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decision.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab   The Sing Dollar was holding above\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7700, with the market focusing on the outcome of SingTel\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  's bid for Australia's Optus .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "With the market still looking long of U.S. dollars we are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concerned that any withdrawal by SingTel will lead to the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar coming off sharply here," Mansoor Mohi-uddin, regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS Warburg said in a research note.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bears had piled up sizable U.S. dollar long positions on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculation SingTel would buy the Australian company at around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $7 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was still less wary of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which threatens the 1.7800\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was on a healthy tone, holding above 44.00 after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore players took profits on their U.S. dollar long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But analysts said the slowing economy and political risks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pointed to a distress for the Thai stock market, thereby for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the dollar was facing resistance at 44.150,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with a break of this bulwark opening the way to near the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par November 26 high of 44.435, which also marks the 38 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par retracement of its steep January 18-April 5 1998 drop, on a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekly chart.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The one-month forward rate in the offshore market eased to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8/13 satang per dollar from 10/12 in late Monday trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won recovered from a fresh 28-month low in line with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains in the yen but trade is likely to remain subdued ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Fed rate decision.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Profit-taking in dollar/yen and overnight Nasdaq gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prompted players to trim their dollar longs against the won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of Korea will release the preliminary 2000 gross\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic product growth data at 0300 GMT. A recent Reuters poll\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par showed economists on average expect the Korean economy to have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contracted by nearly one percent in the fourth quarter from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par third quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab   The peso was steady, aided by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steady yen and a mild recovery in January imports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Philippines imports rose to $2.47 billion in January from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $2.24 in December but it was still below year-ago levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Economists said the bounce from December showed a slowdown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in exports, due to tapering world demand for electronics\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par products, could soon be reversed, at least temporary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said players were looking levels to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sell the U.S. dollar above 48.50, which would underpin the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was down as markets braced for protest rallies\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par planned in the day by supporters of President Abdurrahman Wahid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par who is facing increasing pressure to step down amid corruption\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par allegations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fears that the rallies led by the 40-million strong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nahdlatul Ulama, Indonesia's largest Muslim organisation, could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par add to the violence plaguing the country for the past several\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months were likely to keep the rupiah under pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said given the political situation, moves like\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rate hikes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unlikely to give a lasting support to the rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Indonesia said on Monday it would raise interest rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week due to concerns over inflation and added that it had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continued to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to support the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ailing rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah's recent fall through 10,000 to the U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has unsettled officials, fearful that imported inflation could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raise prices for Indonesia's millions of poor and spark more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par social unrest across the embattled country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar was hovering close to 32.80, its lowest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since January 9 but dealers said rise in the yen and gains in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. tech stocks was likely to keep the downside limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said expected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows in the domestic stocks market, with foreign investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying T$8.327 billion in the last four sessions was also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to provide support.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, trade was likely to remain subdued with most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players staying cautious ahead of the Fed policy meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3k03rbz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
