\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Languish, with all eyes on BOJ, Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 02:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 19 (Reuters) - The dollar dominated Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Monday, but was held in check by a cautious market ahead of two key \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings this week. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan will hold a monetary policy board meeting later in the day amid growing speculation it may return to the zero interest rate policy only six months after abandonning it. \par \par \uc2  Whatever the outcome, few in the market expect the yen to benefit as it struggled to stay off 22-month lows. And the euro continued to come up short as the market's concerns over Japan and the U.S. spilled into Europe. \par \par \uc2  There was also some focus on a Washington summit between Prime Minister Yoshiro Mori and President George W. Bush amid Japanese media reports that they were likely to agree to tolerate a weak yen. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve will meet on Tuesday, and is widely expected to cut the federal funds rate, which currently stands at 5.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  A recent Reuters poll showed the market was split as to how deep the cuts would be, with 13 out of 25 primary dealers of U.S. government securities expecting a 50 basis point cut, while 12 expected a 75 basis point cut. \par \par \uc2  While further easing by the Fed would encourage most regional central banks to continue with their own rate cuts, the outlook for the region remained gloomy given slowing external demand. \par \par \uc2  Last week's OPEC meeting also produced more bad news for Asia as the cartel decided to reduce crude oil production by 1 million barrels a day. \par \par \uc2  With the exception of Indonesia and Malaysia, Asian countries are net importers of oil. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah remained entrenched below the 10,000 mark despite wariness about dollar sales from Bank Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said OPEC's decision to cut oil production was a positive development for Indonesia, but added that domestic political worries were likely to keep the rupiah's upside capped. \par \par \uc2  In the latest round of violence to hit Indonesia, at least 10 people were killed in Aceh province after Jakarta vowed last week to carry out a limited military crackdown against separatist rebels in the region. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it might further raise key interest rates to ease inflationary pressures arising from the weakening rupiah and reiterated it would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Asian Development Bank said on Saturday it was prepared to lend Indonesia between $600 million and $1.2 billion a year over the next three years, provided Jakarta pressed ahead with key policy reforms. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar hit fresh two-and-a-half year lows around 1.7765, a level not seen since September 1998, taking its cue from the weaker yen, Aussie and the euro. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was rather thin, making it easier to push the Sing dollar lower. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that SingTel may not reach an agreement to buy Australia's Cable & Wireless Optus as expected, on Monday, added to the Sing dollar's woes. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the Sing dollar to return to 1.7730 in the short-term as charts showed it was in oversold territory, with a 14-day relative strength index reading at around 83.63. The market is less wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the weakness in the Sing dollar has been in tandem with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso remained the wrong side of 48.00 in early offshore trade, in line with weaker regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the yen. \par \par \uc2  Markets in Manila were keeping a close eye on the Fed's meeting on Tuesday, as the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has indicated it was awaiting the Fed's next move before cutting rates further. \par \par \uc2  The bank left its overnight borrowing and lending rates steady last week at 10.5 percent and 12.75 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2  The government said at the weekend a planned bond issue backed by future income from state-controlled agencies could raise at least 56 billion pesos to help plug the budget gap. \par \par \uc2  The government is forecasting a budget deficit of 145 billion pesos, and has been told by the IMF that maintaining fiscal discipline was key to ensuring further economic progress. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was a breath away from 1,300 in early onshore trade, weighed down by a softer yen ahead of the Bank of Japan's policy meeting and expectations of a rise in oil prices after OPEC's weekend production cut decision. \par \par \uc2  Korea imports almost all its oil requirements and competes with Japan in several export markets. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Nasdaq weakness and uncertainty ahead of the Fed meeting on Tuesday were also likely to keep players cautious. \par \par \uc2  Mansoor Mohi-uddin, UBS Warburg's regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, said with DRAM prices unlikely to rise much in the near future, the long-term target for the won was at 1,400. \par \par \uc2  Stepping up its rhetoric to help the battered won, the Finance Ministry said in a statement "the won's excessive sensitivity to the movements of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not desirable", and it was closely watching the market. \par \par \uc2  It added there were no problems with the supply of dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as the trade account was in surplus while more foreign direct investment inflows were expected this month. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT The baht was down near four-month lows of 44.00, a victim of the weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the baht in oversold territory, with a 14-day relative strength index reading at 73.61, but dealers expected it to test 44.15 in line with the bruised yen. \par \par \uc2  The market was awaiting the release of fourth quarter gross domestic product data, due later on Monday. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll showed the Thai economy was expected to grow around 3.00 percent year-on-year in the fourth quarter compared with 2.6 percent the previous quarter. \par \par \uc2  This would mean growth of about 4.2 percent for the whole of 2000, the same level achieved in 1999. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said any upward surprise in the figures could help trim losses. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate in the offshore market was quoted at 8/11 satang per dollar by 0113 GMT. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR The Taiwan dollar was held hostage to the ailing yen, kicking off the day at 32.73 - its worst level since January 8 - after the yen fell to a fresh 22-month low earlier. \par \par \uc2  Weak DRAM prices also weighed on sentiment. UBS Warburg said DRAM oversupply was likely to drag on until the second quarter as producers seemed reluctant to cut back on output despite global gluts. \par \par \uc2  The market is awaiting February export orders and industrial output data, due on Thursday, for further clues on the state of the economy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the Taiwan dollar to be underpinned somewhat by news of foreign investments rising 40.98 percent in January-February, with major flows going into retail, insurance and publishing. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0129 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.04\tab  122.53\tab    -0.41\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7708\tab  1.7733\tab    +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    32.763\tab  32.683\tab    -0.24\par  Korean won   1296.00\tab 1285.00\tab    -0.85\par  Baht\tab      43.95\tab   43.97\tab    +0.05\par  Peso\tab      48.51\tab   47.97\tab    -1.11\par  Rupiah\tab 10340.00     10250.00\tab    -0.87\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.04\tab  114.45\tab    -6.98\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7708\tab  1.7365\tab    -1.94\par  Taiwan dlr    32.763\tab  32.900\tab    +0.42\par  Korean won   1296.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.47\par  Baht\tab      43.95\tab   43.70\tab    -0.57\par  Peso\tab      48.51\tab   50.75\tab    +4.62\par  Rupiah\tab 10340.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -8.41\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3j03t96\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
