\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Bewitched, bothered, bewildered by yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,165 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 09:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 16 (Reuters) - Emboldened by the yen's fresh bout of weakness, dollar bulls dragged regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower on Friday with the Singapore dollar and Korean won suffering the worst blows. \par \par \uc2  With the yen stumbling below the 122.00 level, the won drooped to a fresh 28-month low and the Sing dollar was driven to 30-month lows, hurt by both the yen and struggling euro . \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also contending with persistent talk of U.S. funds decamping from local bourses and converting to send funds home to compensate for U.S. stock losses. \par \par \uc2  Given the pervasive gloom hanging over regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, jawboning by the authorities barely had any impact. The Korean and Indonesian central banks tried to talk up their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to little avail. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, the market was focused on the Bank of Japan's monetary policy meeting on Monday and the Federal Reserve's meeting on Tuesday. While the Fed is expected to ease its federal funds rate by 50 basis points, speculation is mounting that the BOJ may return to a zero interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2  On the domestic front, Thailand is expected to issue fourth quarter gross domestic product data on Monday. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was trapped below 10,000, despite steady dollar sales from Bank Indonesia (BI) and state banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted selling a small amount of dollars earlier in the session. State banks were estimated to have sold around $20 million on behalf of the authorities. \par \par \uc2  "Just the same old story, BI tries to sell dollars, but the corporate demand (for dollars) is just too much," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  Trading was cautious after news on Thursday that Standard Chartered Bank was fined nearly $900,000 for a breach of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbs. The bank said on Friday the fine was excessive, calling the breach \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  errors. \par \par \uc2  BI later said it may revise the penalty. It also said interest rates were likely to rise further to curb inflationary pressures stemming from the weak rupiah. \par \par \uc2  At its weekly note auction on Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark one-month SBI rate rose to 14.97 percent from the previous week's 14.83 percent. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar got little solace in afternoon trading and was pinned near 1.7730, just off two-and-a-half-year lows of 1.7740 hit overnight. \par \par \uc2  Its weakness in tandem with the yen and the euro lessened concerns about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  carry substantial weighting in the Sing dollar's trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing dollar could test as high as 1.78 in offshore market, when bears could take advantage of thin trading conditions. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's non-oil domestic exports for February are due on Saturday. A Reuters poll of 10 economists showed the headline number rising seven percent on the year in February, thanks to a falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a lower base. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT The baht was pinned near its day lows around 43.98, taking its cue from the weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said dollar offers from Thai exporters lined up around 44 were supporting the downside. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate in the offshore market was 5/10 satang per dollar, down from 8/13 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The bleak mood was further bruised after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspended an unnamed financial institution from the local repo market for 10 days after it breached \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporting rules. \par \par \uc2  Analysts estimated the Thai economy grew around three percent in the fourth quarter compared to a year earlier, bringing 2000 annual growth to 4.2 percent. The figures are due for release on Monday. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso finished at its session high of 48.50 after running into onshore dollar sales from a market long of dollars. \par \par \uc2  After gapping down at the open and slipping to a low of 48.73 on the back of yen-inspired weakness in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso kept within a fairly narrow range. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the bank was sticking with its peso forecast of 46-48 to the dollar for this year. \par \par \uc2  He added that it was possible for the overnight borrowing rate, now at 10.5 percent, to fall below 10 percent, hopefully in the first half of 2001. \par \par \uc2  Socio-economic Planning Secretary Dante Canlas said gross domestic product growth should average 4.7-5.2 percent in the next three years. He said the GDP forecast for this year remained 3.8-4.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won ended not far from a 28-month low of 1,294.5 as the yen's slide prompted offshore players to hedge against further falls in the won. \par \par \uc2  Depressed Korean stocks and dollar buying in the non-deliverable forward market also weighed on the won. The one-month dollar/won NDF was quoted at 1,293/94 in late trade against 1,291.2/91.92 earlier while the six-month was at 1,296.5/98.5 versus 1,294.7/94.95. \par \par \uc2  A Korean government official's comment expressing disapproval of the won's trend of tracking the yen lower failed to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it was not backed by actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The official said Korea was more concerned about a weak won leading to a rise in consumer prices than it was about boosting export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar slipped to a two-month closing low of 32.683 on the back of the losses on the yen and won. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted selling dollars in order to cushion the Taiwan dollar's fall. Bank of America said in a research note it now expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to test 32.70 in the coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan competes with both Korea and Japan on a number of exports, and analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow the Taiwan dollar to weaken to maintain export competitiveness. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0834 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.53\tab  120.93\tab    -1.31\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7727\tab  1.7685\tab    -0.24\par  Taiwan dlr    32.683\tab  32.555\tab    -0.39\par  Korean won   1285.00\tab 1281.70\tab    -0.26\par  Baht\tab      43.97\tab   43.82\tab    -0.34\par  Peso\tab      48.45\tab   47.93\tab    -1.07\par  Rupiah\tab 10325.00\tab 9900.00\tab    -4.12\par 