\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Beaten down by yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,028 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 03:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 15 (Reuters) - Dollar bulls jumped into Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets early Thursday as dollar/yen pushed towards 121 despite repatriation by Japanese companies ahead of fiscal year-end this month. \par \par \uc2  There was also talk that some U.S. funds are selling stocks in the region and sending money back home to make up for losses in their domestic markets. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment was also hurt by the rupiah, which was struggling the wrong side of 10,000 with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  upstaged by political gloom and strong corporate demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Going forward, dealers expected the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade at the lower end of their recent ranges in the near-term as a turnaround in fundamentals was not likely to happen soon. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar/yen punched through 120 for 121 in New York on Wednesday. That, in combination with persistent U.S. equity jitters, should maintain strongly supportive dollar/Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  environment," said IDEAglobal in a research note. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht slid to 43.79 in early trade, its worst level since January 2, as both offshore and onshore players actively bid for dollars in the wake of the yen's renewed weakness. \par \par \uc2  But it was likely to be supported by high baht funding costs in the offshore market, where one-month forwards rose to 10/13 satang per dollar from 6/9 satang late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the dollar/baht was still trapped in an uptrend channel that started on February 15. \par \par \uc2  On the fiscal front, Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said Wednesday preliminary estimates showed Thailand may post a budget deficit around 200 billion baht in 2001/2002 Oct-Sept fiscal year against an expected 105 billion baht in the current year. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLARS \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar lapsed to around 1.7660, after an offshore drop knocked it down to 1.7680, a fresh two-and-a-half year low. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported U.S. names were selling to repatriate funds. \par \par \uc2  The Sing was also feeling pain from the weaker yen, another stumble in overnight U.S. stock markets, and burgeoning mergers and acquisition activity which entails overseas purchases. \par \par \uc2  Singapore brokerage Vickers Ballas Holdings said on Wednesday it was looking for more acquisitions both in Singapore and elsewhere in the region. \par \par \uc2  Any dire performance by the Straits Times Index would further bruise the mood, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A local bank dealer said speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  should keep the downside to 1.77. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was the wrong side of 10,000, with little respite in sight. Bid/ask spreads were also unusually wide, quoted at 10,150/300 at 0125 GMT, which indicated a reluctance to trade. \par \par \uc2  Persistent state bank selling of dollars, believed on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , kept the rupiah away from 30-month lows seen earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah also benefited slightly from expectations that the Indonesian bank agency would convert some $345 million from its sale of palm oil plantations to a Malaysian company. \par \par \uc2  But local corporate demand for dollars amid Indonesia's turbulent political scene continued to pressure the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Indonesia also received a warning from one of its major lenders. Tokyo warned late Wednesday that Jakarta's backsliding on reform could hinder loans from Japan. \par \par \uc2  Japan's total aid disbursement to Indonesia up to March 2000 was 3.92 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was likely to feel pressure on the back of the yen's falls. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to defend the local dollar to slow its fall. The bank was spotted selling dollars on Wednesday around 32.55, and was expected to come in around 32.60. \par \par \uc2  Given the weakness in the yen, dealers said there was some renewed interest in the Taiwan dollar non-deliverable forward market. At 0036 GMT, the one-month Taiwan dollar was at 0.10/13 and the three-month was at 0.28/31. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  Falls in the yen and the Korean stock market dealt a two-fisted blow to the won. \par \par \uc2  For the past few weeks, the won has been tracking the yen closely as Korea competes with Japan on a number of exports to the U.S. Korea also exports a sizable amount to Japan as well, making the won even more vulnerable to the yen's movements. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the local bourse dropped more than three percent at the open in reaction to significant falls on Wall Street as concerns over a gloabl economic slowdown hit a fever pitch. Any signs of foreign fund outflows were likely to further dampen sentiment towards the won. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said dollar selling by exporters may help slow the won's decline. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso ceded ground to 48.34 compared with Wednesday's close of 48.20. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the general weakness in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , depressing stock markets and solid corporate demand for the U.S. dollars dogged the peso. \par \par \uc2  However, they said the downside was supported around 48.45 due partly to fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't think BSP would come right away at this level, but any dips on the peso should be met by BSP," a Manila dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0200 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.80\tab  119.62\tab    -0.98\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7665\tab  1.7600\tab    -0.37\par  Taiwan dlr     32.60\tab   32.52\tab    -0.23\par  Korean won   1287.10\tab 1277.80\tab    -0.72\par  Baht\tab      43.80\tab   43.54\tab    -0.59\par  Peso\tab      48.29\tab   47.14\tab    -2.38\par  Rupiah\tab 10045.00     10110.00\tab    +0.65\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.80\tab  114.45\tab    -5.26\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7665\tab  1.7365\tab    -1.70\par  Taiwan dlr     32.54\tab   32.90\tab    +1.11\par  Korean won   1287.10\tab 1277.00\tab    -0.78\par  Baht\tab      43.80\tab   43.70\tab    -0.23\par  Peso\tab      48.29\tab   50.75\tab    +5.09\par  Rupiah\tab 10045.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -5.72\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3f03vkh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
