\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Steady, but bears poised to pounce. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 09:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 13 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held onto the stronger end of their recent ranges late Tuesday, though bearish sentiment towards the yen and U.S. equities threatened to knock them over. \par \par \uc2  Dramatic falls on U.S. equity markets overnight grabbed the spotlight, and forced most major regional bourses lower. That added some pressure on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said two consecutive sessions of major falls on the technology-heavy Nasdaq did not bode well for Asian economies and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly those dependent on electronics exports such as Taiwan, Korea, and Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Asia from an external perspective continues to suffer. The chain reaction from the exporters, to producers to domestic economies is already coming through...if anything we've not seen the worst yet," said Craig Chan, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ING Barings in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Making matters worse, the yen was still out of favour due to concerns over the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  While it regained some ground during Tuesday's session, traders attributed this to Japanese firms and banks trying to cover losses by converting proceeds from foreign assets, not to renewed confidence. \par \par \uc2  The euro slipped, unable to make much of the troubles facing the U.S. and Japanese economies. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah found its feet below 10,000 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government showered the market with verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop it up after Monday's slide to 30-month lows of 11,210. \par \par \uc2  Local dealers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent around $30 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Tuesday compared with around $12 million on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, chief economics minister Rizal Ramli said the government would support all the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to boost the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  But he said there was no need to impose capital controls or to force exporters to repatriate their dollar earnings. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes the market very cautious. There won't be (strong) dollar buying that we saw in the past few sessions for some time," said a dealer at one foreign bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "But the rupiah would creep lower...gradually because dollar demand is still pretty active," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was unmoved by Foreign Minister Alwi Shihab's comments late Monday, expressing hope about the prospect for progress in talks with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  They said players wanted to see hard signs of progress towards the disbursement of a long-delayed $400 million loan. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar chalked up modest gains in the afternoon to pop above the 1.76 mark, having fallen more than one percent in a week to lows of around 1.7630. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar got some solace as the yen and rupiah recouped losses in afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  Traders also cited dollar sales by local banks, which spurred talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) might be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the Sing dollar's drop. \par \par \uc2  They said that was enough for the market to shrug off a distressing three percent drop in the Straight Times Index , but the outlook for the Sing dollar remained less than rosy. \par \par \uc2  "Singapore is the prominent tech economy. A slowdown in the global technology cycle should contribute to downward momentum in the first and second quarter," a European bank analyst said. \par \par \uc2  This might encourage the MAS to shift its monetary policy bias to neutral from tightening, he added. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht rose and held above 43.70 as the calmer yen and rupiah gave investors a much-needed excuse to pare their very long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  But it ran into resistance from offshore and onshore dollar buying at around 43.62, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market reacted cooly to a newspaper report that Thailand and Japan were close to concluding a bilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap agreement in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  "Perhaps investors might need more details to determine what kind of implications the agreement would have on the market," said a dealer at a local bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  The offshore one-month foreward rate eased slightly to 4/9 satang per dollar from 6/10 satang earlier as players unwound their dollar holdings. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was wedged in a narrow 48.10-48.21 range, tracking regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the absence of strong local leads. \par \par \uc2  It finished at 48.16 in the onshore market on Tuesday, slightly off its opening 48.15 and Monday's close of 48.145. \par \par \uc2  Market turnover was moderate, with $130.80 million traded compared with $138.8 million on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the political front, President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo said new peace talks between the government and the communist National Democratic Front (NDF) would start on April 27. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a local newspaper reported that the government expected tax enhancement measures and higher earnings from privatisation to bring the estimated budget deficit of 145 billion pesos down to 80 billion pesos. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won managed to recoup some lost ground as the yen fended off 20-month lows. \par \par \uc2  That spurred unwinding of long dollar positions, helping the won off a day low around 1,284. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar faced stiff resistance around 1,290 - a level it last hit on January 18 - as exporters were looking to sell dollars below that level. \par \par \uc2  However, with uncertainty lingering over the yen's outlook and the Korean economy, analysts said the won still faced an uphill battle in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  "With the U.S. economy likely to experience a U-shaped recovery rather than a V-shaped rebound, Korea's ecconomy will continue to slow," said UBS Warburg in a research note. \par \par \uc2  It has a near-term forecast for the won of 1,300 and a long-term forecast of 1,400. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar succumbed to the yen's recent losses and faltering regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While the tech-heavy stock market resisted the Nasdaq's fall, the local dollar was under pressure from foreign fund outflows. Dealers in Taipei estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market saw an outflow of around US$100 million on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted defending the local dollar past 32.50. \par \par \uc2  "Around here is going to be a little tough (for the U.S. dollar)," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. "If the yen manages to strengthen a little from here, we're going to have a hard time." \par \par \uc2  Chartists pointed out that the 14-day relative strength index for the Taiwan dollar showed the U.S. dollar was overbought, with a reading of around 85 at 0823 GMT. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0828 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.13\tab  120.38\tab    +0.21\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7586\tab  1.7608\tab    +0.13\par  Taiwan dlr    32.508\tab  32.473\tab    -0.11\par  Korean won   1274.00\tab 1277.20\tab    +0.25\par  Baht\tab      43.56\tab   43.68\tab    +0.28\par  Peso\tab      48.16\tab   48.00\tab    -0.32\par  Rupiah\tab 10200.00     10400.00\tab    +1.96\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.13\tab  114.45\tab    -4.73\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7586\tab  1.7365\tab    -1.26\par  Taiwan dlr    32.508\tab  32.900\tab    +1.21\par  Korean won   1274.00\tab 1277.00\tab    +0.24\par  Baht\tab      43.56\tab   43.70\tab    +0.32\par  Peso\tab      48.16\tab   50.75\tab    +5.39\par  Rupiah\tab 10200.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -7.16\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3d04ahk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
