\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Struggling along as good news eludes. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 02:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 13 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dragged their feet lower in early trade on Tuesday as the beleaguered yen and the battered Indonesian rupiah undermined regional sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The yen, already down 3.0 percent against the dollar this month, pushed to a fresh 20-month low overnight on mounting political uncertainty and Japan's bleak economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could provide some support for the rupiah, but in the absence of fundamental change, analysts said they did not expect to see a meaningful turnaround soon. \par \par \uc2  The country's impasse with the IMF involving $400 million in vital funds is far from being resolved. This could jeopardise a $5.8 billion debt rescheduling deal with the Paris Club of official creditors. \par \par \uc2  A fund spokesman said in Washington that it expected to have future discussions with Indonesian authorities but there were still some major issues to be overcome. \par \par \uc2  Analysts and dealers expect regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to retain their bearish tone in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  "Looking forward, we continue to be most bearish on the yen. For Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we remain bearish especially on the baht, and the rupiah," said a DBS report. \par \par \uc2  "The Sing dollar will continue to face downward pressure due to a weaker yen and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it said. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was underpinned by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which jumped in to sell up to $12 million in the market on Monday to shore up the sagging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the market was also cautious that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might soon tighten its grip on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading to halt a slide in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "I doubt very much if Bank Indonesia would resort to full-fledged capital controls. They might instead do something to force exporters to sell their dollars. The market seems a bit cautious at this point," said a Singapore dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Otherwise, the rupiah could creep lower...it could reach 12,000 because there is no good news whatsoever either from the economic or political front," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it is committed to a free exchange rate regime. \par \par \uc2  President Abdurrahman Wahid, whose leadership is being heavily criticised, said on Monday he would not step down, adding that the country would fall apart if he did. \par \par \uc2  Although Indonesia's spat with the IMF drags on, many believe the Fund will not abandon the country. However, it is expected to stick to its guns on reforms. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht pushed below the 43.70 mark alongside other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as foreign names bought dollars in both spot and forward markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht might soon test 44.00 but not without rounds of dollar profit-taking. The dollar was looking overbought with a reading of 76 on the 14-day relative strength index. \par \par \uc2  But it should find some support at around 43.50 where the market is likely to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dips, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There is no strong local lead at the moment, so the baht seems to be tracking the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The weaker yen and the ailing rupiah have spurred dollar demand and hedging activity," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate was quoted at 1/3 satang per dollar offshore and -11.5/-9.0 satang onshore. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar kept a softer tone to stay just below a three-and-a-half month low of 1.7620. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors unloading the Sing dollar because they expected local equities to follow the U.S. stock markets, which again took a dive on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Weakness in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the euro compounded its woes, they added. \par \par \uc2  "We see various parties are selling. Singapore, Hong Kong, Tokyo, everyone," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said 1.7690 was now within sight, a level not seen since September 1998. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the market was not too concerned about the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Sing dollar, given that its decline was in line with weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its trading partners. \par \par \uc2  One analyst said there was growing speculation the MAS would revise their stance to neutral from a tightening bias soon, which meant the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would guide the Sing dollar lower. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was depressed by losses in the local stock market, the weaker yen, and poor economic data. It opened at 1,284.0 against Monday's close of 1,278.4. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark KOSPI , whose performance usually affects sentiment in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, shed 3.14 percent at the open as investors were unnerved by hefty losses in the Nasdaq overnight. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors sold a net 23.5 billion won worth of shares in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment was also dampened by bleak current account data. Korea's current account surplus was almost halved in January to a provisional $684.4 million from December's final $1.24 billion. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the faltering semiconductor sector, a main export component, would keep pressure on the economy in the months ahead. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO The peso opened a tad lower at 48.15 and was expected to stay pressured by weaker regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with dealers watching how local equities would perform. \par \par \uc2  Another factor upsetting the peso was a $470 million loan held by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which is maturing in April. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said the bank may simply buy dollars from the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the peso to creep lower to 48.35, to fill a gap between 48.25 and 48.35. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar made a soft start, briefly dipping past the 32.50 per dollar mark to lows not seen since end-January as the Nasdaq drop triggered selling of local electronics shares. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the Taiwan dollar fell sharply as recent declines on Wall Street sparked foreign fund outflows, which dealers estimated at US$100 million on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The local dollar's close below 32.40 on Friday prompted speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had moved back its line of defence, prompting the market to push it lower, given the sagging yen and declines in tech stocks. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0145 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.29\tab  120.38\tab    +0.07\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7615\tab  1.7608\tab    -0.04\par  Taiwan dlr    32.477\tab  32.473\tab    -0.01\par  Korean won   1280.00\tab 1277.20\tab    -0.22\par  Baht\tab      43.74\tab   43.68\tab    -0.14\par  Peso\tab      48.18\tab   48.00\tab    -0.37\par  Rupiah\tab 10450.00     10400.00\tab    -0.48\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7997\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.29\tab  114.45\tab    -4.85\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7615\tab  1.7365\tab    -1.42\par  Taiwan dlr    32.477\tab  32.900\tab    +1.30\par  Korean won   1280.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -0.23\par  Baht\tab      43.74\tab   43.70\tab    -0.09\par  Peso\tab      48.18\tab   50.75\tab    +5.33\par  Rupiah\tab 10450.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -9.38\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7997\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3d0481u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
