\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Indonesia  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  directly to buy rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 03:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , March 9 (Reuters) - Bank Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday, selling an estimated $20 million to defend the rupiah around the 9,920/30 level, dealers in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  "We saw Bank Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market this morning at 9,920/30," said a dealer at a foreign bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "There's genuine demand for dollars out there, and Bank Indonesia is the only supplier of dollars in the market. There are no other suppliers," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said several state banks were also spotted in the market selling dollars. State banks have tended to sell dollars on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 9,935/45 to the dollar at 0211 GMT, against levels of about 9,925 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Heavily indebted local companies have been buying dollars in order to repay or service foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have noted that buying has picked up steam in recent sessions as the end of the first quarter approaches and amid growing worries over Indonesia's shaky political and economic outlook. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx39046g8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
