\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Steady, thanks to dearth of factors. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 02:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 7 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were enjoying a breather early Wednesday amid a dearth of fresh factors and dull activity on the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  However, that calm may be broken later in the day with the Thai government set to announce the details of its planned asset management company. Optimism over the AMC was damped recently after reports that it would fall short of initial promises. \par \par \uc2  The yen , which had been the dominant factor in regional markets in recent sessions, see-sawed in early trade. While most analysts are calling for a weaker yen in the coming months, it was drawing support from exporters' dollar sales, fund repatriation, and a market already long of dollars. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro held onto most of its gains from overnight trade. \par \par \uc2  The technology-heavy Nasdaq's 2.87 percent rise may lift sentiment towards North Asian bourses, with possible spillover for their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if foreign investors turn up. Foreign funds bought substantial amounts of Korean and Taiwan shares on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the data front, Taiwan will release its February trade balance at 0245 GMT. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah did not stray far from its levels of late Tuesday, though local corporate dollar demand was expected to pressure it. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta have said state banks have been selling dollars in order to cap the rupiah's slide. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta markets received a rare bit of good news on Tuesday when an Economics Ministry official said a team from the IMF was expected to arrive on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Talks between the IMF and Jakarta have been deadlocked recently over issues ranging from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence to regional autonomy. A mission from the IMF would be an important first step for Jakarta in securing the release of a delayed $400 million loan from the Fund. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia said late Tuesday it was closely monitoring the offshore rupiah non-deliverable forward market. The bank's governor Sjahril Sabirin added that the impact, so far, has not been worrying. \par \par \uc2  At 0043 GMT, the one-month NDF rate was quoted at 10,000/10,050 while the six-month was at 10,650/10,850. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said volume had picked up in recent weeks, though trading was still cautious due to wariness over Bank Indonesia. A dealer at a U.S. bank said interbank players were continuing to deal with transactions of no more than $2 million, which was one of the terms banks originally agreed upon at the market's creation. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar nudged up as players returning from a holiday on Tuesday decided they were too long of dollars. \par \par \uc2  With the yen and Thai baht steadying, dealers said the market was looking to take profits on the dollar around 1.7560/80. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was also supported by Tuesday's local press report quoting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  as saying it was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to balance out any impact of local companies buying assets overseas. \par \par \uc2  "The market is pretty long and there is no strong incentive at this point to further add the dollar to those positions," said a dealer at an Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  "Having said that, there are lots of people out there who would seek to buy the dollar if it dips to 1.7530-1.735. I bet the market will move in a narrow 1.7530-1.7580 range in the near-term," he said. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won opened higher at 1,262.9 compared with Tuesday's close of 1,264.8 as sentiment was boosted by the steadier yen and gains in the stock market. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors bought a net 32.5 billion won worth of local shares in early trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the inflows to the stock market were likely to have limited direct impact on the won as more and more investors were seeking to hedge their positions in the belief economic troubles in Japan would pull the won lower. \par \par \uc2  The market is focused on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy meeting on Thursday. Nine of 10 economists polled by Reuters predicted the bank would leave its short-term rate target unchanged. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht firmed as players covered short positions ahead of the government's annoncement of its AMC plan. \par \par \uc2  Initial news of the AMC plan had bolstered local markets, but recent reports of the plan falling short of initial promises have left some investors disappointed. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, dealers in Singapore said sentiment towards the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the baht, was still bearish. They added 43.20 was still strong support for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Chartists said dollar/baht had been in an uptrend channel since February 13, and a break below 43.20 would move it out of that channel. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was slightly stronger on the back of improving sentiment over the island's tech sector. \par \par \uc2  At 0118 GMT, local stocks were up 2.12 percent, following the Nasdaq and Philadelphia Semiconductor Index's gains overnight. Dealers said foreign fund inflows have provided major support for the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Taipei said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted in the market on Tuesday buying U.S. dollars to cap the local dollar's gains. With a fragile yen and a weaker yen, analysts said the authorities were likely to become more concerned with Taiwan's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan will issue its February trade balance at 0245 GMT. A recent Reuters poll showed economists on average expect Taiwan to post a US$25 million surplus against US$546 million in January. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was quoted at around 47.61/47.67 in early trade in a quiet market, with no deals done more than half an hour after the domestic open. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said on Wednesday he saw the peso averaging 46 per dollar if the U.S. economy could achieve a soft landing. He did not provide a time frame. \par \par \uc2  Salomon Smith Barney said in a report there was scope for the peso to strengthen to 46 if the outcome of the May congressional election favoured President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said with the steadier peso, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to cut its key overnight rates further - a move that could drive the benchmark 91-day T-bill rate below 10 percent. The next monetary policy meeting is on Thursday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0138 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.92\tab  118.45\tab    -0.40\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7540\tab  1.7546\tab    +0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    32.354\tab  32.362\tab    +0.02\par  Korean won   1263.80\tab 1264.80\tab    +0.08\par  Baht\tab      43.40\tab   43.43\tab    +0.07\par  Peso\tab      47.60\tab   4