\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Granted reprieve with steadier yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 6 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  found a stronger footing late on Tuesday as the yen crept back up against the dollar after several Japanese officials expressed concern over its recent decline. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also said the market was heavily long of dollars, and the comments spurred covering of yen positions. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also slightly damped by the yen's recovery. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said concerns over the Japanese economy, which many see as tottering close to the brink of a serious downturn, remained firmly in place. JP Morgan forecasts the yen to hit 120 by end-March and 122 by end-June. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said the pace of Japan's economy was slowing and its outlook was uncertain. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Thai baht, and the Singapore dollar all rode on the yen's coat-tails on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's bleak political scene continued to defeat the rupiah, which slipped back towards 9,900. \par \par \uc2  Trading throughout the region was quiet as Singapore markets were closed for a public holiday, limiting offshore interest in Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar firmed slightly in line with the yen in light offshore trade as local markets were closed for a public holiday. They will re-open on Wendesday. \par \par \uc2  A local newspaper report quoting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  as saying it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to damp excessive exchange rate movements, including those linked to mergers and acquisition flows, also supported the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have attributed the Sing dollar's recent weakness in part to heightened speculation over Singapore Telecommunications' possible bid for Australia's Cable & Wireless Optus . \par \par \uc2  An Australian paper reported on Monday SingTel was almost certain to win the bidding for Australia's second largest telephone firm. That report quoted an unnamed source. \par \par \uc2  Vodafone Group Plc and Telecom Corp of New Zealand are the other bidders for Optus. PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso gave way to corporate dollar demand after hitting an early high of 47.54 per dollar, but dollar offers above 47.80 limited the downside. \par \par \uc2  The Supreme Court's ruling upholding Gloria Macapagal Arroyo's presidency continued to be supportive, but dealers said the peso was likely to face a near-term barrier at 47.50. \par \par \uc2  Salomon Smith Barney said the peso could rally further to 46 per dollar if the outcome of the May congressional elections favoured Arroyo. \par \par \uc2  But it added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to tolerate a much stronger peso due to concerns about export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "Between 46-47 is the dollar/peso range where we believe the BSP may enter the market and arrest the peso's appreciation," Salomon said in a report. \par \par \uc2  Separately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it hoped to conclude the syndication of a three-year term loan worth $740 million by March 15. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won benefitted from the firmer yen, exporter dollar sales and equity purchases by foreign investors, gapping higher at the open after Monday's close at a six-week low of 1,273.3. \par \par \uc2  That put the dollar back into neutral territory on the 14-day relative strength index after Monday's spurt above the overbought mark of 70. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the yen to remain a key driver for the won, given that both countries compete in export markets. \par \par \uc2  "Bank of Korea officials target the won cross rate at roughly 11 against the yen," said Craig Chan, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ING Barings in Hong Kong. Yen/won was at 10.64/66 at 0840 GMT. He noted that non-deliverable forward won rates indicated the market expected the spot rate to remain broadly steady over the next six months to a year. \par \par \uc2  "That is reflective of the credibility of the BOK and also the strong balance of payments which we are continuing to see." \par \par \uc2  The BOK holds its monthly policy meeting on Thursday. Nine of 10 economists polled by Reuters expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its short-term interest rate target unchanged at 5.0 percent after recent data showed mixed signs on the state of the economy. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht recouped some lost ground after the yen's rebound triggered profit taking in the dollar. Trade was subdued as Singapore - its major offshore trading centre - was closed. \par \par \uc2  Lack of progress in a probe into a bomb attack on a plane Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra was due to board over the weekend caused those who overbought the dollar to cut long positions pending further developments, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Investigators established the fire was caused by a bomb explosion, but have not said whether the blast was an attempt to assassinate Thaksin. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs were mostly steady, with the one-month forward rate quoted at 3/5 satang per dollar offshore and -10.50/-9.75 satang onshore. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was jostled around a tight range of 9,850-9,875, caught between local and foreign banks' dollar buying and state banks' dollar selling. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said local and foreign banks were buying dollars on behalf of corporate clients. \par \par \uc2  "It doesn't matter what the state banks sell, genuine demand is still there," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  The dealer added the rupiah found some solace from an Economics Ministry official's comments that an IMF team was expected to arrive in Jakarta on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The mission is seen as an important step for Jakarta towards securing the release of a delayed $400 million from the IMF. That loan was delayed in December due to concerns over a number of issues ranging from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence to regional autonomy laws. \par \par \uc2  Stalled negotiations between the IMF and Jakarta have weighed heavily on already depressed sentiment towards the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Rating agency Moody's Investors Service downgraded its outlook for Indonesia to stable from positive, citing political problems and Jakarta's relations with official creditors. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR The Taiwan dollar gave up earlier gains and closed at the day's low of 32.362 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to buy the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a steadier yen and foreign equity funds provided support for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade. Taipei shares rose after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise rate cut late Monday, its third in three months. \par \par \uc2  UBS Warburg expected the Taiwan dollar to trade in a 32.350-32.450 range in the near future given that equity sentiment remained firm. \par \par \uc2  "But with the yen weak, local exporters are losing competitiveness and the CBC will be forced to let the Taiwan dollar (ease) again in months ahead," it said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0909 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.42\tab  118.97\tab    +0.46\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7543\tab  1.7527\tab    -0.09\par  Taiwan dlr    32.362\tab  32.368\tab    +0.02\par  Korean won   1264.80\tab 1272.00\tab    +0.57\par  Baht\tab      43.39\tab   43.44\tab    +0.12\par  Peso\tab      47.60\tab   47.67\tab    +0.15\par  Rupiah\tab  9875.00\tab 9800.00\tab    -0.76\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7615\tab  3.7995\tab    +1.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.42\tab  114.45\tab    -3.35\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7543\tab  1.7365\tab    -1.01\par  Taiwan dlr    32.362\tab  32.900\tab    +1.66\par  Korean won   1264.80\tab 1277.00\tab    +0.96\par  Baht\tab      43.39\tab   43.70\tab    +0.71\par  Peso\tab      47.60\tab   50.75\tab    +6.62\par  Rupiah\tab  9875.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -4.10\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7615\tab  3.7995\tab    +1.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3604jer\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
