\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late On MAS Fears, Interbank USD Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2001\par 09:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was higher against the U.S. dollar late Friday, on long liquidation of U.S. dollar positions by banks on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT (3:30 am EST), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7448, down from S$1.7466 late Thursday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose to an intraday high of S$1.7485 on cautious buying ahead of the Bank of Japan's policy meeting, and on news that DBS Bank Ltd. was bidding for Korea Exchange Bank's credit card unit. \par \par \uc2  However, fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  at levels above S$1.7480 prompted banks to unwind the long U.S. dollar positions they had built up overnight. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's retreat from a high of Y116.80 also helped push it lower against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the U.S. dollar's upside to be capped at S$1.7470 in London and New York trading later Friday, while it will be well supported by bids at S$1.7420. \par \par \uc2  On the bond market, prices of Singapore Government Securities rose on continued bargain hunting on a weak outlook for local and global interest rates, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In the swap market, interest rate swaps eased on greater receiving interest. \par \par \uc2  The 10-year Singapore government bond yield fell six basis points to 3.55% and the seven-year yield ended four basis points lower at 3.30%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the five-year issue fell three basis points to 3%, while the two-year bond yield fell five basis points to 2.11%. \par \par \uc2  The 10- and seven-year interest rate swaps fell four basis points each to 3.70% and 3.44%, respectively. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank money market, the overnight offered rate was higher on pre-weekend demand for funds while terms rates were steady to lower amid flush liquidity. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                  Late Friday        Late Thursday\par                  bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight       2.3750%  2.5000%   1.5000%  1.7500%\par 3 Month         1.8750%  2.0000%   1.9375%  2.0625%\par 1 Year          2.1250%  2.2500%   2.1250%  2.2500%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010725dx2900m3t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
