\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  driven locally. \b0\par\par\uc2 738 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2001\par 10:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso closed higher at 49.48 against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  opening of 50.00, drawing some support from remittances from \par \par \uc2  overseas workers following the Chinese New Year holiday in the \par \par \uc2  region. \par \par \uc2      Manila dealers said local banks received more than $10 \par \par \uc2  million over the weekend, helping drive the peso to high of \par \par \uc2  49.42 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2      Otherwise, fundamentals remain bleak. \par \par \uc2      Philippine Budget Secretary Emilia Boncodin said on Monday \par \par \uc2  the government would have difficulty funding the 725 billion \par \par \uc2  peso ($14.6 billion) budget for 2001 proposed by the government \par \par \uc2  of former president Joseph Estrada. \par \par \uc2      "We might come close to 200 billion (budget deficit) if we \par \par \uc2  don't do anything, and we said we cannot allow our deficit to \par \par \uc2  be so huge three years in a row," she said. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said despite the peso's post-Estrada rebound, the \par \par \uc2  country's weak exports, a weaker yen and concerns over a \par \par \uc2  ballooning fiscal deficit would pull it below the current \par \par \uc2  level. \par \par \uc2      "The peso is likely to stabilise at close to 50 against the \par \par \uc2  dollar by end-March and then hold at that level through \par \par \uc2  midyear," said David Fernandez, regional economist at JP \par \par \uc2  Morgan. \par \par \uc2      "Beyond that, much will depend on the direction of economic \par \par \uc2  policy. If the new government establishes its reform \par \par \uc2  credentials, there will be some upside potential for the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said in a report. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar rebounded from the intraday low of 1.7495\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on dollar profit taking and fears of potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent declines were overdone,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and there was some speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could step\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in at around 1.7500-1.7600.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But views that the MAS might soon shift its monetary bias\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to neutral from tightening kept the Sing dollar below 1.7400.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The MAS said last week it was reviewing its 2001 inflation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and growth projections given deteriorating external conditions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and would release a policy statement in February.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Friday's CPI data for December shouldn't change this view,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par according to our economists. The headline number came out\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slightly higher than expected at 2.1 percent year/year," UBS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Warburg said in a report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But while this is above the MAS' comfort zone of 1-2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent for CPI, the authorities are likely to focus instead on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the prospect of slowing economic growth in the coming month,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the report said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar faltered as traders returned from an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par extended Chinese New Year break to face a falling stock market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and lingering uncertainty over a nuclear power plant\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par controversy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volumes were light, with many players opting to sit on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sidelines ahead of the Fed rate decision and a meeting of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan lawmakers to decide on a temporary session to review\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par whether to resume construction of a US$5.5 billion nuclear\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par plant.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taipei shares lost nearly three percent on Monday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as a spate of earnings warnings by U.S. firms hit heavily\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weighted tech counters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stuck with its recently relaxed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary stance, with governor Perng Fai-nan saying the bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would adopt an "appropriately loose" monetary policy and would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consider following suit if the Fed cuts rates this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He said the bank would also fully supply funds to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par enterprises, but did not elaborate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trimmed its key discount rate and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par accomodation with collateral rate by 0.125 percentage point on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par December 28 to boost the flagging economy.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0819 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.88\tab  116.65\tab    -0.20\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7485\tab  1.7466\tab    -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    32.525\tab  32.564\tab    +0.12\par  Korean won   1266.00\tab 1279.90\tab    +1.10\par  Baht\tab      42.64\tab   42.78\tab    +0.33\par  Peso\tab      49.44\tab   49.60\tab    +0.32\par  Rupiah\tab  9446.00\tab 9430.00\tab    -0.17\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.88\tab  102.21\tab   -12.55\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7485\tab  1.6640\tab    -4.83\par  Taiwan dlr    32.525\tab  31.380\tab    -3.52\par  Korean won   1266.00\tab 1135.00\tab   -10.35\par  Baht\tab      42.64\tab   37.45\tab   -12.17\par  Peso\tab      49.44\tab   40.20\tab   -18.69\par  Rupiah\tab  9446.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -26.16\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1t0768p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
