\par\par \b \uc2  Politics grips rupiah, Taiwan dollar easier. \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2001\par 03:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0235 GMT - The Indonesian rupiah drifted lower as local companies bought dollars, but dealers said its downside was limited by a lack of selling from offshore due to a liquidity squeeze. \par \par \uc2  - Market eyeing politics with parliament committee due to report to legislature on Monday the result of its probe into two financial scandals linked to President Abdurrahman Wahid. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta dealers said demand for dollar from corporate sector active, but market cautious ahead of meeting between foreign banks and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected later on Monday to discuss complex new \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules aimed at curbing rupiah speculation. \par \par \uc2  - Taiwan dollar easier on first trading day after long Chinese New Year holiday due to uncertainty over nuclear power plant controversy and interest rate outlook. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Perng Fai-nan said on Monday bank would adopt loose monetary policy, but did not elaborate. \par \par \uc2  - Thai baht traded above 42.80 amid talk market participants continuing to unwind long Sing dollar/baht positions as political dust settling. \par \par \uc2  - Analysts say market watching for formation of new government after results of Monday's re-votes are known. \par \par \uc2  - "The re-elections won't have any impact on the market because we don't expect them to at all change the political equation. The market just wants to know when the new government will be in place. Any further delay would be baht-negative," said Bangkok dealer. \par \par \uc2  - Offshore one-month forward rate easier at -3.8/0.2 satang per dollar while onshore rate of same tenor steady at -10.50/-8.50 \par \par \uc2  - Singapore dollar recouped some early losses in thin market on U.S. dollar profit-taking around 1.7480. Despite some retracement, dollar/Sing still trading near overbought territory with reading of 69.5 on 14-day relative strength index. \par \par \uc2  - Dealers said Sing dollar's recent losses overdone and there's fear \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1.7500. \par \par \uc2  - But speculation MAS might soon shift its monetary bias to neutral from tightening keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below 1.7400. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1t07661\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
