\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Uninspired by 2nd Fed cut, yen weighs. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2001\par 03:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly easier in early trade on Friday after the U.S. Federal Reserve's second discount rate cut in two days failed to excite the market. \par \par \uc2  Players chose to focus instead on the beleaguered yen which slid to a 16-month low, as well as on domestic political and commercial leads. \par \par \uc2  The Fed on Thursday cut the largely symbolic U.S. discount rate by an additional quarter percentage point to 5.5 percent, just one day after it surprised the market by slashing its key federal funds rate by 50 basis points and discount rate by 25 basis points. \par \par \uc2  The move occurred after the New York close, leaving little room for U.S. markets to react. \par \par \uc2  "In theory, the cut should provide some support to Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the immediate term. But again, there are lots of other factors that are driving the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the Southeast Asian ones," said Syetarn Hansakul, economist at WestLB in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "And there are some in the market who now suspect the surprise move by the Fed might indicate something is going terribly wrong somewhere, or the economic situation in the U.S. is much worse than previously anticipated," she said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the dollar to retain its toehold above 116 yen as Japan's sluggish economy came into focus amid fading euphoria over the Federal Reserve's rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  The euro held comfortable above 95 cents and 110.00 yen , supported by growing optimism about the outlook for European economies compared to Japan and the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Markets are keenly awaiting the U.S. employment report for December, due at 1330 GMT. Economists polled by Reuters see non-farm payrolls adding 102,000 jobs after adding 94,000 in November. \par \par \uc2  The unemployment rate is expected to inch up to 4.1 percent from a 4.0 percent reading in November, and would be the second straight month it has risen. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was under renewed pressure as local equities slipped on the back of more losses in U.S. technology shares. \par \par \uc2  While the won had mustered some strength on Thursday, there was good support for the dollar just below 1,250, where buying interest, especially from local oil importers, kicked in. That onshore dollar demand was expected to remain in Friday's session. \par \par \uc2  Dollar buying in the non-deliverable forward market overnight, particularly in the shorter-dated tenors, also pressured the spot exchange rate. The one-month won was at 1,272/74 compared with 1,241 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  And the won's near-term prospects were dimming, analysts said. Despite the initial cheer from the Fed's rate cut on Wednesday, Korea is more affected by the direction of U.S. economic growth rather than the direction of interest rates, said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  With that in mind, the implication of the Fed's rate cuts - that the authorities have become increasingly concerned about U.S. growth - was hurting the won, he said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar weakened as players bought the U.S. dollar back after overselling it on Thursday, with the yen's fall past 115 intensifying buying interest for the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  The yen is believed to have accounted for around 15 percent in Singapore's trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which the Sing dollar is managed against. "Yesterday, the Sing shot up to 1.7270 where dollar demand kicked in again as some became short. There was also fear of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a U.S. bank dealer in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Looking at trade flows today, I think the Sing's upside will be capped at 1.7300 where dollar bargain hunting orders are lining up, while the support is seen at around 1.7380 - a level the market failed to break last night in New York," he said. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was still straddling the 9,500 mark, with local corporate demand for dollars expected to keep the dollar buoyed. \par \par \uc2  While Indonesian rates have been creeping higher over the past several months, mainly to defend the rupiah, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Miranda Goeltom said on Thursday it would not seek an excessively tight monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  However, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said earlier on Thursday the bank would not cut rates following the Fed's move to lower key U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Sabirin faces a long-awaited graft trial on January 17 on charges that he was involved in the Bank Bali scandal . \par \par \uc2  He returned to work late last year after spending nearly six months in detention over his alleged involvement in the scandal, which caused international lending agencies to suspend loan disbursements to Indonesia and destroyed the re-election chances of former president B.J. Habibie. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's Attorney General's office also questioned a former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Soedrajad Djiwandono on Thrusday about billions of dollars of controversial loans made in the late 1990s. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was softer against the dollar despite the second Fed rate cut on Thursday which was overshadowed by the ailing yen and political uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  But the unit found some support around 43.50 where a Singapore name and a European name out of London emerged to offer the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Thais will be voting to choose the new government on Saturday. However, analysts reckon the general elections this weekend will not put an end to the political uncertainty gripping the country but merely prolong it. \par \par \uc2  Telecoms tycoon Thaksin Shinawatra is still well ahead in most opinion polls despite being indicted by Thailand's anti-corruption agency for failing to declare some of his wealth. \par \par \uc2  The concern is that Thailand could plunge deeper into political uncertainty if Thaksin becomes the next premier because he will be removed from office if found guilty by the Constitutional Court. \par \par \uc2  One-month forward rate was quoted at -3.0/-1.0 satang per dollar offshore and -13.2/-11.5 satang onshore. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso slipped past the 51 per dollar mark in early offshore trade in line with weakness in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dealers in Manila said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could test lower levels on uncertainty ahead of the Thai general election. \par \par \uc2  "We think the peso can test 51.50-60 as there will be some nervousness in the market ahead of elections in Thailand," a dealer at a local bank in Manila said. \par \par \uc2  Philippine markets closely watch movements in the Thai baht as Thailand is considered to be a competitor in exports. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to change its key overnight rates in its weekly policy meeting later in the day, given poor inflation data released early Friday. \par \par \uc2  Consumer prices rose 6.6 percent year-on-year in December, against a rise of 6.0 in November, higher than market expectations of a 6.4 percent rise. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura on Thursday said the bank would discuss a 50-100 basis point rate cut at Friday's meeting. The benchmark overnight borrowing rate now stands at 13.5 percent and lending rate at 15.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said lower interest rates were needed to boost the stagnant economy but could also fuel inflation already on the rise because of a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and high energy prices. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said news the Equitable-PCI Bank had suffered considerable withdrawals of funds after being embroiled in the impeachment trial of President Joseph Estrada would also keep sentiment depressed. \par \par \uc2  Equitable has handed over documents to the trial court which have indicated the presence of a 500 million peso trust account allegedly opened by Estrada. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar dipped below the 33 per dollar mark, depressed by a weaker yen and won but dealers said fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited further losses. \par \par \uc2  They said a higher opening of the local stock market, helped by a second cut by the Fed in its discount rate, also kept players from pushing the local dollar lower. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said easing concerns of a hard landing in the U.S. would help sentiment, but Taiwan's slowing growth and exports and a weak financial sector were likely to weigh on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday said the cuts in U.S. rates would help stabilise the local dollar and allow Taiwan to keep monetary policy loose. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan will release its December consumer and wholesale price indices at 0300 GMT. November CPI rose 2.26 percent year on year while the wholesale price index up 2.51 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0205 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.64\tab  114.38\tab    -1.94\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7355\tab  1.7320\tab    -0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    33.015\tab  32.948\tab    -0.20\par  Korean won   1272.00\tab 1251.60\tab    -1.60\par  Baht\tab      43.46\tab   43.37\tab    -0.20\par  Peso\tab      51.08\tab   50.82\tab    -0.51\par  Rupiah\tab  9520.00\tab 9502.00\tab    -0.19\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.64\tab  114.39\tab    -1.93\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7355\tab  1.7365\tab    +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    33.015\tab  32.900\tab    -0.35\par  Korean won   1272.00\tab 1277.00\tab    +0.39\par  Baht\tab      43.46\tab   43.70\tab    +0.55\par  Peso\tab      51.08\tab   50.75\tab    -0.65\par  Rupiah\tab  9520.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -0.53\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1505qa6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
