\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Firmer, but Fed rate cut cheer fading. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2001\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 4 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held their ground late Thursday, though they gave up early, showier gains as markets considered the implications of the Federal Reserve's surprise rate cut. \par \par \uc2  The Fed cut its key federal funds rate by 50 basis points to six percent on Wednesday amid increasing signs of a harder than expected landing for the U.S. economy. It also cut its more symbolic discount rate by 25 basis points. \par \par \uc2  While global markets, particularly equity markets, were relieved by the much-hoped for easing, some analysts said the earlier than expected cut showed the Fed had fallen behind the economic curve. \par \par \uc2  Others said there was a whiff of desperation about the move, which may point to a more dire economic outlook for the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, with the exception of Indonesia and the Philippines, joined in the initial euphoria over the rate cut with the Korean won and Thai baht leading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore, Bangkok, and Hong Kong said the slight rebound in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more due to narrowing rate differentials than the prospect of rate cuts by regional authorities. \par \par \uc2  While analysts expected North Asian central banks to follow suit with their own monetary easing, lower interest rates would do little for the more severely hobbled economies of Indonesia, the Philippines, and Thailand - all of which are wracked by political turmoil as well. \par \par \uc2  "The beneficiaries (of the rate cut) will be those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold off due to the concerns over global economic growth, being the Taiwan dollar and Korea won," said David Simmonds, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "But it (the rate cut) doesn't impact the elections in Thailand, nor the impeachment trial in the Philippines. Nor does it address the enormous political complications in Indonesia." \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won managed to end on a stronger note despite paring early gains as local importers bought dollars, taking advantage of its low levels. \par \par \uc2  Gains on the local stock market boosted the won, with foreign investors buying a net 395 billion won worth of shares on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign direct investment in Korea for the full year 2000 rose one percent on year to hit $15.7 billion, with the government saying foreign direct investment could top $15 billion this year if labour issues were settled and corporate restructuring carried out. \par \par \uc2  That, however, has been the problem, analysts have said. Korean financial markets have been roiled in recent weeks by a raft of external and domestic problems - from slowing global demand for exports and firm oil prices to the agonisingly slow corporate reform process and a spate of labour union strikes. \par \par \uc2  While an easier monetary policy would help Korea deal with an expected economic slowdown, a number of issues remain, especially corporate and financial reforms, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was weaker, having ceded all of its earlier gains, and then some, as U.S. names covered short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a European bank in Singapore said a large foreign investment bank based in Hong Kong was also spotted buying dollars in late Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  The baht, along with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had rejoiced over the Fed's rate cut, and firmed through the psychological 43 level earlier in the day, triggering stop-loss dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Bangkok said the baht had initially benefited from a narrowing differential between Thai and U.S. interest rates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, said later its interest rate policy would not be affected by the U.S. rate cut. \par \par \uc2  Thailand has maintained a low rate policy to boost sluggish domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  But local companies as well as offshore players snapped up dollars at the intraday lows, dealers in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Finance Minister Pisit Leeahtam said earlier in the day the baht would recover after the January 6 elections, supported by Thailand's strong fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Prime Minister Supachai Panitchpakdi chimed in, saying thin volumes were aggravating the baht's recent volatility. \par \par \uc2  While some dealers in Bangkok said the market had already priced in a victory by Thaksin Shinawatra's Thai Rak Thai (TRT) Party, concerns over continued political uncertainty were lurking. Thaksin was indicted last week of corruption charges, and faces a five-year ban if found guilty. But a final court decision could take months. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar held its gains as the stock market built on early Wall Street-driven momentum to end nearly five percent higher, further encouraged by parliament's adoption of Taiwan's 2001 budget. \par \par \uc2  The Fed rate cut also helped, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying it would help stabilise the local dollar and allow Taiwan to stick to a loose monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  It did not specify whether Taiwan would follow suit with more cuts, a week after trimming the discount rate 0.125 percentage point to 4.625 percent. \par \par \uc2  Parliament adopted the government's 2001 budget, whittling away T$32.66 billion after a marathon session plagued by political wrangling. \par \par \uc2  It authorised spending of T$1.5755 trillion, a moderate four percent rise over 2000, but two percent below the T$1.6082 trillion proposed by the cabinet. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar shed its gains as players took profit on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it failed to break 1.7250 on fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon to curb its rapid appreciation. \par \par \uc2  But dealers expected it to be well-supported around the current level on talk Solectron Corp , which bought a 33 percent stake in Natsteel Electronics , was still unwinding up to $300 million to acquire the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Singapore's Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) for December showed a reading at 52.5 percent, down 2.8 points from the previous month. \par \par \uc2  The composite index is based on indicators measuring orders, production, inventories and stocks of finished goods. \par \par \uc2  On the monetary front, analysts said they did not expect the the Fed's rate cuts to affect Singapore's interest rates much, partly because the MAS had started tightening its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy since last year. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , through its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is taking liquidity out of the system which would prevent interest rates from falling," said Vincent Low, fixed income strategist at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The onshore peso market ended a breath away from the 51 per dollar mark, giving up early gains as political and economic uncertainty depressed sentiment. \par \par \uc2  It reached a day high of 50.79 from Wednesday's close of 51.04 following gains by other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the back of the Fed rate cut and Nasdaq rally. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a turnaround in the U.S. economy would ease some of the pessimism on the economic front as the U.S. is the largest consumer of Philippine electronics exports. \par \par \uc2  Exports in the first 11 months of 2000 grew 7.8 percent against the year-ago period to $34.582 billion. In November alone, exports came in at $3.317 billion against $3.075 billion in November 1999. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the country posted a balance of payments deficit of $532 million in the first nine months of 2000, a sharp deterioration from its surplus of $65 million in the first eight months. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said political uncertainty, as the impeachment trial against President Joseph Estrada drags on, was likely to keep sentiment negative. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the Monetary Board would discuss a 50-100 basis point cut in key overnight rates at its Friday meeting. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the bank faced a dilemma as rate cuts were needed to stimulate the economy, but the peso was likely to suffer from increased liquidity. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah firmed back past the 9,500 level as some players trimmed long dollar positions ahead of a review process with the IMF on the next letter of intent starting on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts expect the IMF to finally give a go ahead to the next tranch of loans to Indonesia despite an initial delay. \par \par \uc2  Late last month, local media reported the Fund might not issue fresh loans of around $400 million until the passage of key amendments to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. \par \par \uc2  The disbursement of funds from the IMF - which agreed to loan Indonesia $5 billion over three years to help mend its crisis-hit economy - is tied to a series of economic reforms. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said strong corporate demand for the dollar was likely to keep the rupiah below 9,500 in the near-term. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0900 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     114.62\tab  114.58\tab    -0.03\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7319\tab  1.7305\tab    -0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    32.948\tab  33.033\tab    +0.26\par  Korean won   1256.30\tab 1270.00\tab    +1.09\par  Baht\tab      43.35\tab   43.48\tab    +0.29\par  Peso\tab      50.82\tab   51.00\tab    +0.35\par  Rupiah\tab  9500.00\tab 9520.00\tab    +0.21\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     114.62\tab  114.39\tab    -0.20\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7319\tab  1.7318\tab    -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    32.948\tab  32.992\tab    +0.13\par  Korean won   1256.30\tab 1263.00\tab    +0.53\par  Baht\tab      43.35\tab   43.35\tab    -0.01\par  Peso\tab      50.82\tab   49.90\tab    -1.81\par  Rupiah\tab  9500.00\tab 9625.00\tab    +1.32\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1406wss\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
