\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  easier in quiet end-year trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 506 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2000\par 07:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0600 GMT - Most regionals drift in weak ranges amid a low volumes on the last trading day of the year. \par \par \uc2  - Korean won -2 hovers in choppy trade around 1,263 day low as lack of expected dollar selling by local banks encourage offshore players to pull it down. \par \par \uc2  - But some dealers still expect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support in 1,265-70 range. \par \par \uc2  - Sentiment also helped on end of seven-day strike by Kookmin Bank and Housing and Commercial Bank staff against merger agreement of the two banks. \par \par \uc2  - Six-month NDFs rise to 1,260/63 from early 1,251.5/53.5. One-year NDFs at 1,262/65 from 1,253.0/55.0. \par \par \uc2  - More signs of slowing economy as industrial output fall 1.0 percent seasonally adjusted in November from September due to decrease in domestic consumption and exports. \par \par \uc2  - November output up 6.4 percent year-on-year, but down from a 29 percent year-on-year gain in November 1999. \par \par \uc2  - Government statement said gross domestic product 2001 target between five to six percent, against current year's estimated growth of 9.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  - Commerce ministry sees trade surplus down to $10 billion in 2001 from $12 expected in 2000. \par \par \uc2  - Thai baht depressed on political uncertainty and modest dollar demand from corporates but month-end exporters' inflows help cap downside at around 43.40. \par \par \uc2  - Tuesday's anti-graft tribunal indictment of January 6 poll front runner Thaksin Shinawatra deepen uncertainty on post-election scenario. \par \par \uc2  - Thaksin faces five-year ban from politics but constitutional court needs to confirm indictment which may take months and raises possibility of throwing out elected prime minister if Thaksin wins. \par \par \uc2  - Baht funding cost also easing offshore with one-month forwards at discount of -3.0/1.0 satang per dollar from premium of 5.0/9.0 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  - Indonesian rupiah slips in offshore trade in line with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Onshore markets closed for Eid Al Fitr holidays. \par \par \uc2  - Dealers in Singapore said offshore players selling rupiah on recent declines in baht and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  - But fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely to cap downside at around 9,600 level. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar moves in narrow 1.7295-1.7330 range with downside capped by year-end exporters and local corporates. \par \par \uc2  - Dealers said players expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to start pushing Singapore dollar higher next week after release of 2000 gross domestic product growth data early next week. \par \par \uc2  - Official estimate at 9.5 percent year-on-year. Reuters poll in early November projected 9.42 percent. \par \par \uc2  - Analysts said relatively strong performance of the Singapore economy to encourage authorities to push Singapore dollar higher against trade-weighted basket. \par \par \uc2  - Philippine peso hovers around 50 level in lacklustre trade as market awaits fresh leads when impeachment trial against President Joseph Estrada resumes next week. \par \par \uc2  - Taiwan dollar hold steady at around 33.15 levels after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doubles reserve ratio for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits resulting in inflows from banks and prompting exporters to cash their earnings. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwct08z1q\par }\p