\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Rises To 15-Week High On Dlr Liquidation \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2000\par 09:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar reached a 15-week high against the U.S. dollar Friday, despite fears that the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might again enter the market to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Trade was thin ahead of the weekend and holidays period, adding to the market's volatility. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7275 down from S$1.7312, late Thursday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was benefitting from the U.S. dollar's weakness against the euro, the Australian and the New Zealand dollars also, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar gained despite fears of another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which, traders suspect, bought U.S. dollars late Thursday at around S$1.7270. \par \par \uc2  In the bond market, the yield on Singapore government bonds was unchanged ahead of the holiday season amid very light trading. \par \par \uc2  Bond prices have risen in recent months and banks are comfortable holding bonds at current levels at least until the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the 10-year paper was 4.11%, the seven-year bond yield was 3.81% and the five-year bond yield at 3.48%, all unchanged. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the overnight offered rate rose to 5.5% from 2.75%. Demand is usually high ahead of the weekend and holidays. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Friday        Late Thursday\par        