\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -SE Asia cheers in dozy, holiday trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2000\par 03:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 21 (Reuters) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were firmer early Thursday, benefiting mostly from pre-holiday unwinding of long dollar positions in thin markets, and slightly from global dollar weakness. \par \par \uc2  The dollar and yen have been groaning under the weight of growing pessimism over the Japanese and U.S. economies, making Europe a more attractive investor destination for now. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the recent dollar sell-off had helped Southeast Asian markets a bit as any dollar sales in illiquid markets would mean a big shift in the exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  And sticking to the trend in recent weeks, North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were smarting from their economies' exposure to the U.S. and the Nasdaq's misfortunes. \par \par \uc2  Downgrades of tech heavyweights Cisco Systems and International Business Machines sent U.S. blue chips and tech shares far south, with the Nasdaq dropping 7.12 percent. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts say Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have steadied in recent sessions due to low liquidity and easing demand for dollars from local corporates. \par \par \uc2  They point out that the political risk situation in Indonesia and the Philippines has not changed. And in Thailand, it could worsen if the front-runner of the January 6 polls Thaksin Shinawatra is indicted by the country's anti-graft watchdog. \par \par \uc2  Other analysts also note that markets in Southeast Asia have priced in much of the bad news already and have been predominantly long on dollars. \par \par \uc2  Players in these markets recently have been unwinding stale long dollar positions, giving these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a boost. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar reaped the benefits of a stronger euro, briefly breaching the 1.7300 mark in early trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing dollar was likely to extend its gains as Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowly inched higher. \par \par \uc2  They added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not seen as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to cap the local dollar's gains as the Sing dollar had not appreciated excessively against its trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Chartists say the Sing dollar needs to break resistance of 1.7275, which it touched on November 3 and 6, but has not breached since early September, before seeing further gains. \par \par \uc2  That area also cuts in near the 62 percent Fibonacci retracement of the U.S. dollar's broad August 10-November 24 rally. It has almost entirely retraced its steep run-up through November. \par \par \uc2  However, on the 14-day Relative Strength Index chart (RSI), the U.S. dollar was skimming the 30 level, with any move below that level indicating it is oversold. INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah slipped back the weak side of 9,200 despite early dollar offers from onshore and offshore names, and from state banks which were spotted selling from 9,200. \par \par \uc2  Although some players stepped in to buy the U.S. unit on dips, the bids were broadly outnumbered by offers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It's not clear if the state banks sold dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. Some were seen unwinding long U.S. dollar and Sing dollar positions against the rupiah," said a dealer at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "One U.S. fund was also heard selling dollars through onshore banks," he said. \par \par \uc2  Chief economics minister Rizal Ramli said on Wednesday Indonesia's approval of new foreign investment projects reached $14.6 billion in the first 10 months of this year, a jump of 35.2 percent from the same period last year. \par \par \uc2  A total of 1,286 foreign investment projects were approved in that period compared with 1,164 in the same period a year ago. \par \par \uc2  Charts show the dollar/rupiah, which had burst into overbought territory on many occasions since September 12, is just a whisker away from oversold territory with a reading of 33.23 on the 14-day RSI. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht nudged higher in early thin trade, supported by dollar offers from interbank players seeking to cut losses and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Despite the baht's recent rapid gains, dealers said it was likely to be capped in the near-term at 42.50 - a barrier it has failed to break since October 10. \par \par \uc2  The IMF's bullish comments about the economy on Thursday were likely to provide further support to the baht. \par \par \uc2  The Fund Thailand's external vulnerability had been much reduced since the 1997-1998 crisis and four to five percent growth was achievable next year if confidence returns after the January 6 election. \par \par \uc2  It also expressed support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's accomodative stance given tame Thai inflation. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won skipped past its support level of 1,220 to hit a year low of 1,223.4 per dollar in early trading as local sentiment was sideswiped by the Nasdaq's losses. \par \par \uc2  Skittish investors have been wringing their hands over the downturn in the electronics sector, which makes up a bulk of Korea's exports. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, trouble at home in the form of labour unrest and the government-led corporate and financial restructuring has depressed local investors' spirits in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  However, Singapre dealers said the move downwards happened in a thin market, meaning the rate was vulnerable to any shift. \par \par \uc2  They added that the market was extremely cautious given that state banks sold off dollars heavily at 1,220 on December 1, sparking talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said offshore players were targeting 1,280 before year-end were behind the dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  He added that there was no sign yet that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, though he expected it to send out a verbal warning later in the day. \par \par \uc2  Some traders also mentioned that players were trying to push dollar/won up in the hope of triggering option positions with a strike price of 1,300, but activity in the options market was very light overall. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar buckled as local stocks took a tumble following further losses on the Nasdaq. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finally gave into mounting pressure of falling stocks and softer \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Taiwan's two biggest competitors, Korea and Japan, on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased its determined defence of the local dollar at the 33.10 on Wednesday, but added that it had been detected in the market on Thursday trying to cushion the Taiwan dollar's fall. \par \par \uc2  Some dollar buying in the non-deliverable forward market by offshore parties has also turned up the pressure on the spot market. \par \par \uc2  Longer-dated tenors in the NDF market were all higher, with the six-month Taiwan dollar NDF at 1.0/1.1, the nine-month at 1.07/1.12 and the one-year at 1.12/1.25. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso yawned through a sluggish session in the morning, with interbank players as major participants. The first deal worth around $1.0 million was taken at 50.50. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to trade in a narrow range in the near-term amid a dearth of trading incentives. \par \par \uc2  "People are already in holiday mood. They intend to celebrate their Christmas and they don't care what else is going on in the world," said a local dealer. \par \par \uc2  Political problems were also expected to be put on a slow burner for now. The impeachment court decided earlier this week to take a break starting next week on President Joseph Estrada's corruption trial, ensuring the outcome of the trial will not be known until next year. \par \par \uc2  Supreme Court Chief Justice Hilario Davide said the trial would resume on January 2. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0210 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     112.92\tab  112.84\tab    -0.07\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7292\tab  1.7344\tab    +0.30\par  Taiwan dlr    33.175\tab  33.129\tab    -0.14\par  Korean won   1223.00\tab 1217.00\tab    -0.49\par  Baht\tab      42.45\tab   42.74\tab    +0.68\par  Peso\tab      50.04\tab   50.00\tab    -0.08\par  Rupiah\tab  9280.00\tab 9220.00\tab    -0.65\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     112.92\tab  102.21\tab    -9.48\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7292\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.77\par  Taiwan dlr    33.175\tab  31.380\tab    -5.41\par  Korean won   1223.00\ta