\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mostly easier, North Asia worst hit. \b0\par\par\uc2 899 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2000\par 02:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and Taiwan dollar were expected to stay in the limelight in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Thursday after recent substantial losses. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's strength against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bolstered by better-than-expected third quarter gross domestic product numbers, would also weigh on the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There had been some speculation that U.S. third quarter GDP growth would fall below two percent, but the figure came in at 2.4 percent, though it was still the slowest pace of growth in four years. \par \par \uc2  Concerns over a domestic loan scandal in Korea, Nasdaq-inspired losses in local stocks and jitters over the corporate sector and economic outlook are weighing against the won. \par \par \uc2  In Taiwan, dealers expected some technical rebound after the local dollar hit a 19-month low of 33.20, but any reprieve could be brief as pressure from political and banking sector worries rose. \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on the other hand, were relatively subdued. \par \par \uc2  The Philippines' financial markets are closed for Bonifacio Day, and will resume trading on Friday. Dealers expected offshore trade to be thin in the light of political uncertainties. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht was also expected to have a subdued session as offshore players remained cautious although onshore banks had cleared gridlock in the past week. \par \par \uc2  The problem was triggered by banks scrambling to pare credits to offshore counterparties down to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's limit of 50 million baht, just before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to strictly enforce existing curbs and imposed a hefty penalty on those who violated them. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was holding just the right side of 33 per dollar and some dealers said they suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was defending the unit. \par \par \uc2  With the Nasdaq hitting its lowest close in over a year, Taiwan's heavyweight technology stocks were under assault, though buying from government-linked funds kept the benchmark index cushioned. \par \par \uc2  Losses in the stock market and an expected slowdown in Taiwan's economic growth have been weighing on the Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  It slid to its lowest since April 1999 on Wednesday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped back from its defence of the 33 level. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the bank has little choice but to allow a steady depreciation in order to compete amid slowing exports demand. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said with the more pessimistic forecasts for Taiwan's economy, offshore players have been actively buying dollars in the non-deliverable forward market. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/Taiwan dollar NDF points were at 0.23/27 while six-month NDFs were at 0.43/47. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah slipped past the 9,500 per dollar level to lows last seen on November 21 on active corporate demand for dollars. Its losses were exaggerated by thin trading volumes and dealers expected it to trade in a 9,500-9,600 range on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A convincing break of 9,570, which has been repeatedly tested but not breached since October 1998, would expose the rupiah to severe declines, chartists said. \par \par \uc2  The market seemed to have ignored a rosy forecast by the government which on Wednesday revised the 2001 target for growth to five percent from the original forecast of 4.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  But it also revised up its 2001 inflation forecast to 7.2 percent from 7.0 percent earlier. \par \par \uc2  In the banking sector, the government said on Wednesday it would issued so-called staple bonds on December 8 which banks can swap with their recapitalisation bonds, some of them at a higher rate. \par \par \uc2  The move is to stimulate investor interest and help calm fears of looming fiscal trouble when the recapitalisation bonds - whose rates are too low to encourage a secondary market - start to mature in a few years. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar eased in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though dealers said the market was reluctant to test the 1.7600 level due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears. \par \par \uc2  They also said local banks sold the U.S. dollar around the 1.7564 level overnight, pushing the Sing dollar to a high of 1.7539. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar is managed against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and often moves in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A weaker yen and baht specifically were weighing on the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  Despite fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the powerful \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said the Sing dollar would grind lower as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the euro remained fragile. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0143 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     