\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late; Tracks Weaker Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2000\par 09:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was lower against its U.S. counterpart late Wednesday, in line with weaker Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0756 GMT (2:56 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7564, up from S$1.7540 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened higher, but off its overnight high of S$1.7582, and traded in a tight S$1.7555-S$1.7575 range through the day. \par \par \uc2  "The (U.S.) dollar's strength in Asia has given it a bid tone against the Singapore dollar," a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said buying interest by local companies is expected to support the U.S. dollar around S$1.7520-S$1.7525 in the near-term, with initial resistance around S$1.7580. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar faces much stronger resistance around S$1.7600-S$1.7620 on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On the bond market, prices of Singapore Government Securities rose sharply across the board, tracking strong gains in U.S. Treasurys overnight. \par \par \uc2  Bond yields fell by four to five basis points. The yield on the 10-year bond ended four basis points lower at 4.21%. The seven-year yield bid fell five basis points to 3.90%. The five-year yield also ended five basis points lower at 3.52%. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, term rates were mostly flat while the overnight rate eased amid flush liquidity. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesda