\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weak bias persists, won wins reprieve. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2000\par 10:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 24 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a mixed bag late Friday, with some winning a reprieve from recent losses, though domestic political uncertainties and a hazy economic outlook still held sway. \par \par \uc2  With U.S. markets closed for the Thanksgiving holiday on Thursday, firm DRAM prices and a rise in Nasdaq futures helped most Asian equity markets post gains and supported their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Korean won, battered in the past few days, saw the most volatile session in the region. \par \par \uc2  It slid through the 1,200 psychological support and later, helped by stock market gains and some positive news on the political front, made its way back up wiping out the early losses. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said more weakness was expected in the coming months as growth and exports were likely to slow down throughout the region, while political unease in several countries was likely to stretch well into the first quarter of next year. \par \par \uc2  A broadly stronger U.S. dollar was also likely to keep the regionals under pressure. \par \par \uc2  The dollar held near nine-month highs against the yen and close to one-month highs against the euro . \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won rebounded from a 13-month low of 1,207 on profit-taking on a heavily overbought U.S. dollar and on news of an end to the political stalemate delaying a key reform bill. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/won came off from overbought levels of 94.5, not seen since January 1998, on the 14-day relative strength index. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the profit-taking in dollars got a further boost after the main Korean opposition party decided to end a parliamentary boycott and support a government bill for 40 trillion won in public funds for financial sector reforms. \par \par \uc2  A 3.21 percent rise in the KOSPI on the back of technology stocks also helped sentiment in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said worries about the fate of the restructuring drive amid threats of a nationwide labour strike on December 5 would cap won gains. \par \par \uc2  And the troubled Daewoo Motor was again facing insolvency after it failed to convince its labour union to agree on job cuts as part of a rehabilitation plan. \par \par \uc2  "The Korean won remains vulnerable given the backdrop of corporate and financial restructuring uncertainties and heavy dollar buying by oil importers," said Standard Chartered in a weekly research note. \par \par \uc2  The bank cut its six-month forecast for the won to 1,380 from 1,150 and said a break of 1,200 would set it on track for a near-term test of the 1,230-1,250 area. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht failed to firmly break through 43.50 resistance, though dollar selling from U.S. investment banks rescued it from a low of 43.97. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Bangkok said the selling pressure on the dollar from offshore players caught short on the baht to fund forward positions was still evident. However, they added that pressure was expected to taper off next week. \par \par \uc2  One-month offshore forwards were at 7.0/15.0 satang to the dollar at 0819 GMT against 5.0/10.0 satang earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  With importers' dollar-buying keeping the dollar buoyed, a dealer at a local bank in Bangkok said 43.40 was strong resistance for the baht. \par \par \uc2  He added that with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  buckling in North Asia, as well as the weaker yen, the baht was likely to fall towards the 44 level in the short term. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was holding comfortably away from the 33 level, with a little help from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened stronger after closing at a 19-month low on Thursday, but then quickly headed south. Dealers in Singapore said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came into the market in full force at 32.99, hauling the Taiwan dollar back onto its feet. \par \par \uc2  They added that given the heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , estimated at $150-$250 million, local players in Taipei decided to take profit on the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  But analysts say the cards are stacked against the Taiwan dollar. Besides negative external factors such as a slowing U.S. economy, a downturn in the electronics cycle and a weaker yen, Taiwan is dealing with a raft of domestic woes. \par \par \uc2  Among them are political squabbling between the DPP president and the KMT-dominated parliament and rising bad loans. \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered said it now expected the Taiwan dollar to hit 35 in the next six months, though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to draw a line in the sand around 33 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Third-quarter gross domestic product data was expected later on Friday. Analysts polled by Reuters expected third quarter GDP to have expanded by 6.29 percent on the year. SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was back near its day lows of 1.7592 per dollar again after rebounding earlier to around 1.7560 on dollar profit-taking and a large Sing dollar order from a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they had not detected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence despite the Sing dollar's overnight decline past a longstanding support of 1.7575/80 where the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said recent weakness in the yen, euro and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which are believed to be components in Singapore's trade-weighted basket, might be making the authorities more tolerant of a weaker Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  UBS Warburg said in a daily research note that Singapore's consumer price index for October had also posted a lower than expected 1.8 percent year-on-year rise, suggesting inflation was not a pressing concern. \par \par \uc2  "...fears about the MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the Sing dollar (and hence monetary policy) seem unjustified at present. As such we look for dollar/Sing to reach 1.7600-1.7650 before the MAS comes in," it said. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fought shy of the 9,500 per dollar level, tracking a tight range between 9,440 and 9,480 amid a lack of fresh leads. \par \par \uc2  The saga over the recapitalisation and board reshuffle at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained in focus, with players awaiting parliamentary approval of changes to laws governing the bank. \par \par \uc2  Chief economics minister Rizal Ramli said on Thursday that the proposed changes were needed to restore accountability and credibility and were not an attack on the bank's independence. \par \par \uc2  He said the government should have reformed Bank Indonesia before granting it independence a year ago, given its performance record in the aftermath of the crisis. \par \par \uc2  BI deputy governor Achjar Iljas, one of only two deputies who did not resign from the board last week to pave the way for a reshuffle, said the bank needed the backing of parliament and the government to clear the aura of scandal surrounding it and solve its massive debt woes. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said uncertainty over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's role and leadership would only undermine the rupiah if it persisted. \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered Bank said in a that a break of the 9,570 support, which has been tested but held since October 1998, would establish a 24-month inverted head and shoulders pattern, creating a new weakening trend. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso ended flat at 49.39 to the dollar in the onshore market after touching a day low of 49.73. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a lull on the political front ahead of the formal start of President Joseph Estrada's impeachment trial had lowered trading interest. \par \par \uc2  "The market is moving on flows alone. There is very little trading interest and even interbank deals are very few," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Manila. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said inflows from overseas workers were supporting the peso while bouts of dollar buying by corporates and foreign banks were capping the upside. \par \par \uc2  They said the dollar purchases by foreign banks were believed to be on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is seen as replenishing foreign reserves spent in defending the peso last month. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its weekly monetary board meeting decided not to change key overnight rates, saying the decision to cut rates hinged on November inflation numbers and stability of the peso. \par \par \uc2  November inflation data is due on December 5. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  jacked up its overnight rates by four percentage points last month saying it was a temporary measure in defence of the peso. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0936 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     111.06\tab  110.17\tab    -0.80\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7587\tab  1.7540\tab    -0.27\par  Taiwan dlr    32.875\tab  32.931\tab    +0.17\par  Korean won   1188.00\tab 1193.00\tab    +0.42\par  Baht\tab      43.77\tab   43.80\tab    +0.07\par  Peso\tab      49.25\tab   49.25\tab    +0.00\par  Rupiah\tab  9455.00\tab 9417.00\tab    -0.40\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     111.06\tab  102.21\tab    -7.97\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7587\tab  1.6640\tab    -5.38\par  Taiwan dlr    32.875\tab  31.380\tab    -4.55\par  Korean won   1188.00\tab 1135.00\tab    -4.46\par  Baht\tab      43.77\tab   37.45\tab   -14.44\par  Peso\tab      49.25\tab   40.20\tab   -18.38\par  Rupiah\tab  9455.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -26.23\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7997\tab    -0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbo00kj1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
