\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late On Korean Won Declines \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2000\par 10:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was lower against the U.S. dollar in late trading Wednesday, tracking developments in the Korean won and the New Taiwan dollar///./// \par \par \uc2  Around 0845 GMT (3:45 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7570, up from S$1.7552 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar had hit a high of S$1.7570 in intraday trading for the second straight day - its highest level since Oct. 31 when it touched S$1.7578. \par \par \uc2  But the small gains turned into losses when the Korean won hit a new year low, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's recent push toward the S$1.7600 level stirred speculation in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the MAS would probably tolerate the Singapore dollar at current levels because the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also weakened against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Yields on Singapore government securities were mixed in light trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the 10-year bond rose to 4.30% from 4.28% in very tight trading, while the yield on the seven-year bond rose to 4.03% from 4.00% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Still, much of the trading focused on the shorter end of the yield curve as investors adjusted their portfolios ahead of a S$2 billion, two-year Singapore government bond offering that opens Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight offered rate fell to 2.2500% from 2.5000% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesday     Late Tuesday\par                   bid      offer     bid      offer\par Overnight         2.2500%  2.3750%   2.3750%  2.5000%\par 3 Month           2.5625%  2.6875%   2.6250%  2.7500%\par 1 Year            2.7500%  2.8750%   2.7500%  2.8750%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwbm05l3d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
