\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Rebounds From 3-Wk Low On Commercial Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2000\par 10:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar strengthened modestly Tuesday as commercial buying interest helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rebound from a three-week low. \par \par \uc2  Around 0930 GMT (4:30 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7552, down from S$1.7558 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar had hit a high of S$1.7570 in intraday trading Monday, its highest level since Oct. 31 when it touched S$1.7578. \par \par \uc2  Volume was thin and the Singapore dollar's appreciation was the result of normal commercial buying for trade purposes, a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  "It was really not much, just the daily ups and downs of the market," he said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's recent push toward the S$1.7600 level stirred speculation in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the MAS would probably tolerate the Singapore dollar at current levels because the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also weakened against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Yields on Singapore government securities eased in light trading, dealers said. The yield on the 10-year bond fell to 4.28% from 4.30%, while the yield on the seven-year bond fell to 4.00% from 4.02% \par \par \uc2  In the money markets, rates were higher as demand for funds increased as players rushed to cover positions ahead of a market holiday in the U.S. Thursday, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight offered rate rose to 2.5000% from 2.1250% Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Tuesday       Late Monday\par                   bid      offer     bid      offer\par Overnight         2.3750%  2.5000%   2.0000%  2.1250%\par 3 Month           2.6250%  2.7500%   2.5625%  2.6675%\par 1 Year            2.7500%  2.8750%   2.6875%  2.8125%\par -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 421-4859;\par alan.yonan@dowjones.com\par -0- 21/11/00 09-38G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwbl05n74\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
