\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Dollar Up Late, But Off High; Bonds Down \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2000\par 09:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was higher against the U.S. dollar late Monday, but gave up its early gains after local companies rushed in to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0836 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7315, down from S$1.7339 late Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened lower in Asia, following its losses against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in New York Friday. Its early losses against the Thai baht pushed the U.S. dollar to an intraday low of S$1.7295. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's brief move below S$1.7300 attracted local companies to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing it to around S$1.7330. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again came close to testing the S$1.7300 level after that European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro following two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday. Corporate buying resurfaced on the post-ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  dip. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said demand from \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  companies will support the U.S. dollar near-term around S$1.7290-S$1.7300, with strong resistance at S$1.7350. \par \par \uc2  On the bond market, Singapore Government Securities fell as some market participants adjusted their positions following Friday's sharp fall in U.S. Treasurys, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Though the overnight offered rate eased to 2.8750% from 4.75% Friday, it stayed above its normal 2.0%-2.5% range indicating relatively tight liquidity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The longer term interest rates were mostly steady, however. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the 10-year bond rose one basis point to 4.27%, while the seven-year bond yield ended two basis point higher at 4.01%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Thursday           Friday\par                   bid      offer     bid      offer\par Overnight         2.7500%  2.8750%   4.5000%  4.7500%\par 3 Month           2.5000%  2.6250%   2.5000%  2.6250%\par 1 Year            2.6875%  2.8125%   2.6875%  2.8125%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwb605azu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
