\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down Late;MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Limit Losses \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2000\par 11:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar slipped late Wednesday as it succumbed to the weakness of its regional counterparts, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar, however, remained capped below S$1.7570 as market participants were wary of provoking another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to have defended the Singapore dollar through several banks between S$1.7560 and S$1.7580 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0855 GMT (4:55 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7560, up from S$1.7533 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  "The market may slowly try to push up the U.S. dollar," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is set to face resistance around S$1.7590 in London and New York trading hours Wednesday, while finding support around S$1.7540, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Despite fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely tolerate some weakening of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it maintains a neutral policy stance for the rest of the year. \par \par \uc2  The MAS, which rarely comments on its actions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, will likely step in to smooth out any excessive movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, but any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't expected to be aggressive for the rest of the year, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts expect the U.S. dollar to rise to S$1.7600 soon if the MAS sits on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  Trading in Singapore government bonds was subdued, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  High oil prices, a slump in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the weak performance on Wall Street overnight fueled selling in Singapore government bonds in early trading, but the yields remained well supported by buying interest, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the 10-year paper was unchanged from late Tuesday at 4.39%. \par \par \uc2  In the interbank market, bids for the overnight rate recovered to 2% from 1.6250% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesday    Late Tuesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         2.0000% 2.3125%   1.6250% 1.8750%\par 3 Month           2.4375% 2.5625%   2.4375% 2.5625%\par 1 Year            2.6250% 2.8125%   2.6250% 2.7500%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4809;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwai051j1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
