\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Revived by Nasdaq, still vulnerable. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Koetsawang \par \uc2 973 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2000\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 16 (Reuters) - Asian stocks danced to the \par \par \uc2  Wall Street beat in early trade on Monday, but closed off the \par \par \uc2  day's best levels due to lingering worries over high oil prices \par \par \uc2  despite the Palestinian-Israeli summit. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The benchmark Nikkei\tab    ended more than one percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher while Seoul shares gained 4.86 percent and Bangkok\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shares finished up more than three percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But stocks in Taiwan sank to a 20-month low due to concerns\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over falling prices of DRAMs, one of the island's major\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Political drama in the Philippines roiled its financial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets, causing the peso to plunge to a new life low of 48.95,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks to shed more than two percent and spreads of its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-denominated bonds to widen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It is still going to remain a situation with a lot of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uncertainty in that country and that will keep investors very\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nervous about holding (the Philippine) assets," said Rebecca\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Patterson, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PESO OUTLOOK BLEAK\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite some reprieve on Monday, analysts expected emerging\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to remain vulnerable to further declines, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par several houses revising down their year-end target for some\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , particularly the peso and the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Patterson said JP Morgan now expected the dollar/peso to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hit 52 as soon as year-end and the dollar/baht to reach 45 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the same time frame.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "First of all, we do think political uncertainty in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippines is going to continue, even though impeachment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par charges against President Joseph Estrada are not filed,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Patterson said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Adding to downward pressure on the unit were the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ballooning budget deficit plus external factors such as bashing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of global stocks and high oil prices, and the fact that some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players still carry long peso positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I think it is very easy to see further peso falls. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par question is how fast and how far can it go," Patterson told\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SHORT BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The weakness in the peso is likely to also drag the Thai\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht lower, with most strategists still recommending their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par clients short the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said its low yield and the Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hands-off policy made the baht an attractive funding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "What we have seen in the last several weeks is investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par who want to have some short exposure to the region and are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par looking around and finding that negative carries are very high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Indonesia and the Philippines," Patterson said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The baht is the one outlier. You have lower yield. And you\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that has a track record of not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nearly as much as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," she\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Patterson suggested clients continue to take long Korean\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won positions against the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Salomon Smith Barney, which just revised its three-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht forecast to 45 from 44, also suggested that clients long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar against the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "In terms of positioning, we maintain the view that long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar is advisable against Thai baht on a one- to three-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par horizon," said David Simmond, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at the bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREA AT BOTTOM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some analysts believed Korean stocks were looking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attractive again, with return on equity (ROE) improving. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOSPI has shed around 46.49 percent since the end of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We look at corporate balance sheets and corporate ROE to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par see whether or not we have seen the return on equity (come\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back) in Korea. Actually we find that it has improved\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dramatically," said Sadiq Currimbhoy, equity strategist at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Merrill Lynch.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I have a sense that the market is very oversold. And the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fact we are seeing the return on equity improve going forward,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that means the market is forming a bottom," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Currimbhoy said the country's largest cellular phone\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par service SK Telecom would be one of a few\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par telecommunications stocks that would drive the market high up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from its bottom.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0920 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     108.07\tab  107.76\tab    -0.29\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7515\tab  1.7545\tab    +0.17\par  Taiwan dlr    31.990\tab  31.920\tab    -0.22\par  Korean won   1127.00\tab 1129.00\tab    +0.18\par  Baht\tab      43.18\tab   43.62\tab    +1.02\par  Peso\tab      48.67\tab   48.40\tab    -0.55\par  Rupiah\tab  8870.00\tab 8940.00\tab    +0.79\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     108.07\tab  102.