\par\par \b \uc2  Sing dlr docile as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk haunts market. \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2000\par 09:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 13 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar shuffled along in a narrow range in Friday afternoon trade as fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  left many traders on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said local banks had been seen selling U.S. dollars around the early high of S$1.7575, spurring talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authority. \par \par \uc2  An MAS spokeswoman declined to comment on the speculation, but the quasi \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said in the past it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out any excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2  "I doubt people will be aggressive (in selling Singapore dollars) for a while," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  It was quoted at 1.7533/43 against the U.S. dollar at 0713 GMT, little changed from its late Thursday levels. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the local dollar should come under renewed attack as a tricky combination of sinking equities and rising oil prices continued to drag down regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Over the past two weeks, the Singapore dollar has been weakening alongside the Thai baht and Philippine peso, which are under intense pressure due to domestic political turmoil. \par \par \uc2  In addition, increasing violence in the Middle East has sent crude oil rocketing to prices not seen in 10 years. Most Asian countries, with the exception of Indonesia and Malaysia, are net importers of oil. \par \par \uc2  The MAS said in July it was prepared to allow a gradual, modest appreciation of the Sing dollar on a trade-weighted basis, reminding the market that containing inflation remained a key objective. \par \par \uc2  DBS Bank said in a report the Sing dollar should strengthen to around 1.72 by the end of the fourth quarter, citing strong economic figures, the MAS's desire to cap inflation, and an expected soft landing of the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  But the head of treasury at a local bank said a slowdown in the United States was still worrisome for regional economies. \par \par \uc2  With U.S. technology companies issuing profit warnings in recent weeks, he said a possible softening of electronics demand would hurt Singapore's economy, and in turn, its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said the Sing dollar could touch lows of around 1.76, not seen since September 4, 1998, by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwad047ez\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
