\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  talk keeps Sing dlr from 25-month low. \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2000\par 04:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 13 (Reuters) - Talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the Sing dollar rebound from close to a 25-month low of 1.7600 on Friday, but dealers said violence in the Middle East and weakness in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep the unit under pressure. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some local banks were spotted selling U.S. dollars around the early high of S$1.7575. \par \par \uc2  The move sparked talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and sent players scrambling to cover their short Sing positions, leaving dollar/Sing bid at around 1.7520 at 0235 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "There were some local banks selling U.S. dollars, so it could be on behalf of the authorities," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore kept to its policy of not commenting on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It is \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy not to comment on market rumours," an MAS spokeswoman told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said in the past that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out any excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2  It was last believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the Sing dollar fell to 22-month lows in July. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  jolted markets soon after by saying it was prepared to allow a gradual, modest appreciation of the Sing dollar on a trade-weighted basis, reminding traders that containing inflation remained a key objective. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar's latest bout of weakness came amid declines in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Philippine peso skidding through a series of record lows and the Thai baht at a 28-month trough. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep players cautious for now, but they expected some spillover from markets panicking around the world on the prospects of the Middle East situation turning into a wider conflict. \par \par \uc2  "Whenever there is talk of war people go for U.S. dollars. So I would say there are more chances of dollar/Sing moving up," the European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Oil prices jumped to decade highs in near-panic trading on Thursday, rocking global markets after violence escalated in the Middle East and peace efforts hit the wall. \par \par \uc2  Technical analysts said the Sing dollar's next support was at 1.7600, a level not seen since September 4, 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwad046md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
