\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Lower Late; Peso Again Leads Falls \b0\par\par\uc2  By Benjamin Pedley \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2000\par 10:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Friday the 13th lived up to its reputation. \par \par \uc2  An escalation of violence in the Middle East rocked global equity markets, ignited a savage oil price rally, and drove all Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. Faced with severe downward pressure, most regional central banks either \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or threatened to step into the market to support their local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso led the decliners again, falling for a fifth straight session on a deepening political scandal surrounding allegations President Joseph Estrada received millions of dollars in payoffs from illegal gambling operators. \par \par \uc2  Political instability has triggered capital flight this week from the Philippines, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday to increase its overnight interest rates four percentage points, lifting the headline rate to 15%. \par \par \uc2  Although the peso ended the week at Thursday's all-time intraday low against the dollar of PHP48.500, the rate hike has at least stabilized the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has fallen 6% during the past four weeks, and 17% so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Rising crude prices also hurt the peso. \par \par \uc2  The Philippines like most Asian economies - including South Korea, Thailand and India - is heavily dependent on oil imports for its energy needs. \par \par \uc2  So a surge in oil prices on fears supplies might be interrupted if violence in the Middle East escalates into an all-out war between Jews and Arabs is particularly damaging for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  An apparent bombing of the U.K. embassy in Yemen early Friday crystallized those concerns, and some analysts said this could be a precursor to concerted attacks on Western interests. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at PHP48.500, up from PHP47.700 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was weaker despite apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the day by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the MAS bought Singapore dollars against its U.S. counterpart through a number of local banks at around S$1.7570, pushing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to around S$1.7520. But the effect was short-lived as weakness in the peso and rupiah, and a 2.7% fall in the benchmark Straits Times Index of local stock prices knocked the Singapore dollar from its intraday highs. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at the European bank said: "The Sing dollar is surrounded by bad news. No matter what authorities do, sentiment is still weak and won't just change overnight." The MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a number of times above S$1.7500 in recent months to curb weakness in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was inspired at that time by falls in the rupiah due to political problems in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar late was at S$1.7550, up from S$1.7523 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  In neighboring Indonesia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it is considering whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the rupiah, which hit a 10-week low early in the day of IDR9,030 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We will need to evaluate what caused the rupiah weakness before we make a direct move in the market," said Bank Indonesia senior official Achjar Ilyas. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia Acting Governor Anwar Nasution has previously said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would defend the rupiah at IDR9,000, arguing that beyond this level it is grossly undervalued compared to economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at IDR8,955, up from IDR8,940 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Bank of Thailand acknowledged for the first time there are signs of speculation against the baht in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, activity that as a general rule might prompt a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Chetthavee Charoenpitaks, assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, told reporters the Bank is closely monitoring movements in the market, but declined to comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the baht. \par \par \uc2  The baht hit a 28-month low Friday of THB43.68 against the dollar, and late in the session was at THB43.580, down from THB43.295. \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, the Korean won sank as local stock prices slumped 1.9%. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended trade in Seoul at KRW1,128.5, up from KRW1,122.10 late Thursday. While in Taipei, the New Taiwan dollar dropped sharply to finish the week at NT$31.650 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , down from NT$31.300 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  -By Benjamin Pedley, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4485; ben.pedley@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwad04z3c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pic