\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Falls To 10-Wk Low Vs USD At IDR9,030 \b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2000\par 02:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah early Friday sank to a 10-week low against the U.S. dollar at IDR9,030, dragged lower by weakness in the Thai baht and expected falls in the Philippine peso. \par \par \uc2  Trade in Manila started at 0100 GMT. At around 0111 GMT the dollar was trading PHP48.200, according to Bridge Telerate, up from Thursday's close of PHP47.700 on the Philippine Dealing System Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The peso hit an all-time low Thursday at 48.50 pesos against the dollar on a deepening political scandal. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah hasn't traded beyond IDR9,000 since July 31. \par \par \uc2  The level of IDR9,000 is significant because Bank Indonesia Acting Governor Anwar Nasution last month pledged to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this level. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of neighboring \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier Friday to buoy the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Benjamin Pedley, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 421 4806;\par benjamin.pedley@dowjones.com\par -0- 13/10/00 01-13G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwad04y4o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
