\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down Late; Intel Adds To Won Woes \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 799 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 11:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened late Friday, after a profit-warning from U.S. semiconductor giant Intel Corp. sent many regional bourses reeling, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The warning dealt the hardest blows to the South Korean won and the New Taiwan dollar, given the importance of semiconductor chips for these countries' exports, analysts said. The increasingly pessimistic outlook on the semiconductor sector has exacerbated the short-term prospects of these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have recently been weakening on other domestic concerns. \par \par \uc2  But heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept a rein on the New Taiwan dollar's decline, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar wasn't unscathed. The U.S. dollar briefly crossed above the critical S$1.75 resistance as the local stock market index skidded to a four-month low on Intel's announcement. \par \par \uc2  Intel said late Thursday it expects its third-quarter revenue to fall below previous expectations, primarily because of weaker demand in Europe. \par \par \uc2  The won, which had already been weakening on falling prices of computer chips, one of South Korea's biggest export items, skidded to as low as KRW1,134.90 to the dollar minutes after the open on Intel's warning. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at KRW1,134.70, higher than Thursday's close of KRW1,128.10, as the local stock market tumbled 7.2%. \par \par \uc2  The won, has been on a steep decline since last Friday, when Ford Motor Co. said it had aborted its bid for Daewoo Motor. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is poised to extend its downward spiral in coming weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is poised to test its upside target of KRW1,140 soon, they added. \par \par \uc2  But Thio Chin Loo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas Group, said a lot of the bad news has already been priced in the won, which is expected to trade between KRW1,120 and KRW1,140 against the dollar in the short term. \par \par \uc2  "If stability returns to the stock market, the dollar will trade at the lower end of its trading range," she said. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at NT$31.295, up from Thursday's close of NT$31.263, in dealings valued at US$428 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around US$150 million throughout the day to stem the New Taiwan dollar's losses, but it failed to overcome the pressure from heavy foreign equity fund outflows, which contributed to a 4.5% plunge on the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  The slump in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets dragged the Philippine peso to a new record closing low while the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stayed absent from the local market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 46.155 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up from PHP45.995 Thursday and just off its intraday high of PHP46.165. \par \par \uc2  The peso's weakness had sparked debate about pegging the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but such a move appears unlikely. \par \par \uc2  Opposing a senior lawmaker's call that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least consider a peg, Finance Secretary Jose said Friday the government opposes capital controls and has no plans to implement a peg to stabilize the peso. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the selloff on the Singapore bourse and the fall in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  accelerated the Singapore dollar's descent in late trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  With no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cracked above the crucial level of S$1.75, market participants pushed the U.S. dollar to S$1.7523 around 1000 GMT (6:00 a.m. EDT), up from S$1.7460 late Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have defended the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 24 at around S$1.7515 against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  With the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hitting fresh 27-month lows, the psychological support level of 43 baht to the dollar is expected to give way next week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had climbed to THB42.945, from THB42.67 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Strong onshore dollar demand; expensive oil prices and mounting political anxieties ahead of the country's general elections, expected later this year, continued to pressure the baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to 8,805 rupiah against the dollar, from IDR8,792 late Thursday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers are waiting to see if the weekend meeting of finance ministers and central bankers from the Group of Seven leading industrial nations will come up with concrete measures to salvage the euro, which has consistently been falling to new lows against both the dollar and the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9m04ngs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
